lane-head" x="316" y="-8" text-anchor="middle">SR</text><text class="lane-head" x="532" y="-8" text-anchor="middle">LLR</text><text class="lane-head" x="748" y="-8" text-anchor="middle">TC</text><g class="cell sn" data-id="SN-002" tabindex="0" style="--ring:#ffffff"><title>SN-002 — The trace from need → requirement → design → test is mechanically verified, not manually asserted: every requirement links to a need and a test before a gate.</title><rect x="0" y="0.0" width="200" height="17.0" rx="3" fill="#4338ca"></rect><text x="100" y="9.0" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central"><tspan x="100" dy="0">SN-002</tspan></text></g></svg></div><div class="layer" data-layer="archl-sn-003" hidden><svg viewBox="0 -22 848 40" width="848" style="width:100%;max-width:848px;min-width:526px;height:auto" preserveAspectRatio="xMinYMin meet" role="group"><text class="lane-head" x="100" y="-8" text-anchor="middle">SN</text><text class="lane-head" x="316" y="-8" text-anchor="middle">SR</text><text class="lane-head" x="532" y="-8" text-anchor="middle">LLR</text><text class="lane-head" x="748" y="-8" text-anchor="middle">TC</text><g class="cell sn" data-id="SN-003" tabindex="0" style="--ring:#ffffff"><title>SN-003 — The kit is stack-agnostic — a non-Python project uses it by re-pointing the harness at that stack&#x27;s tools, with Python only as the reference.</title><rect x="0" y="0.0" width="200" height="17.0" rx="3" fill="#4338ca"></rect><text x="100" y="9.0" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central"><tspan x="100" dy="0">SN-003</tspan></text></g></svg></div><div class="layer" data-layer="archl-sn-004" hidden><svg viewBox="0 -22 848 40" width="848" style="width:100%;max-width:848px;min-width:526px;height:auto" preserveAspectRatio="xMinYMin meet" role="group"><text class="lane-head" x="100" y="-8" text-anchor="middle">SN</text><text class="lane-head" x="316" y="-8" text-anchor="middle">SR</text><text class="lane-head" x="532" y="-8" text-anchor="middle">LLR</text><text class="lane-head" x="748" y="-8" text-anchor="middle">TC</text><g class="cell sn" data-id="SN-004" tabindex="0" style="--ring:#ffffff"><title>SN-004 — Progress advances only through explicit approval gates (G1→G2→G3→…), and a gate passes only when its mechanical bar is met.</title><rect x="0" y="0.0" width="200" height="17.0" rx="3" fill="#4338ca"></rect><text x="100" y="9.0" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central"><tspan x="100" dy="0">SN-004</tspan></text></g></svg></div><div class="layer" data-layer="archl-sn-005" hidden><svg viewBox="0 -22 848 40" width="848" style="width:100%;max-width:848px;min-width:526px;height:auto" preserveAspectRatio="xMinYMin meet" role="group"><text class="lane-head" x="100" y="-8" text-anchor="middle">SN</text><text class="lane-head" x="316" y="-8" text-anchor="middle">SR</text><text class="lane-head" x="532" y="-8" text-anchor="middle">LLR</text><text class="lane-head" x="748" y="-8" text-anchor="middle">TC</text><g class="cell sn" data-id="SN-005" tabindex="0" style="--ring:#ffffff"><title>SN-005 — AI agents and humans work from the same playbook, with the process enforced agent-neutrally (git hooks + CI), not by trusting any one agent.</title><rect x="0" y="0.0" width="200" height="17.0" rx="3" fill="#4338ca"></rect><text x="100" y="9.0" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central"><tspan x="100" dy="0">SN-005</tspan></text></g></svg></div><div class="layer" data-layer="archl-sn-006" hidden><svg viewBox="0 -22 848 40" width="848" style="width:100%;max-width:848px;min-width:526px;height:auto" preserveAspectRatio="xMinYMin meet" role="group"><text class="lane-head" x="100" y="-8" text-anchor="middle">SN</text><text class="lane-head" x="316" y="-8" text-anchor="middle">SR</text><text class="lane-head" x="532" y="-8" text-anchor="middle">LLR</text><text class="lane-head" x="748" y="-8" text-anchor="middle">TC</text><g class="cell sn" data-id="SN-006" tabindex="0" style="--ring:#ffffff"><title>SN-006 — An agent can run unattended and resume from repo text alone; such a run never blocks on a prompt and fails clearly.</title><rect x="0" y="0.0" width="200" height="17.0" rx="3" fill="#4338ca"></rect><text x="100" y="9.0" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central"><tspan x="100" dy="0">SN-006</tspan></text></g></svg></div><div class="layer" data-layer="archl-sn-007" hidden><svg viewBox="0 -22 848 40" width="848" style="width:100%;max-width:848px;min-width:526px;height:auto" preserveAspectRatio="xMinYMin meet" role="group"><text class="lane-head" x="100" y="-8" text-anchor="middle">SN</text><text class="lane-head" x="316" y="-8" text-anchor="middle">SR</text><text class="lane-head" x="532" y="-8" text-anchor="middle">LLR</text><text class="lane-head" x="748" y="-8" text-anchor="middle">TC</text><g class="cell sn" data-id="SN-007" tabindex="0" style="--ring:#ffffff"><title>SN-007 — The kit&#x27;s own changes stay traceable and tested — a change to a script is covered by a test exercised end-to-end against a real scaffold.</title><rect x="0" y="0.0" width="200" height="17.0" rx="3" fill="#4338ca"></rect><text x="100" y="9.0" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central"><tspan x="100" dy="0">SN-007</tspan></text></g></svg></div><div class="layer" data-layer="archl-sn-008" hidden><svg viewBox="0 -22 848 40" width="848" style="width:100%;max-width:848px;min-width:526px;height:auto" preserveAspectRatio="xMinYMin meet" role="group"><text class="lane-head" x="100" y="-8" text-anchor="middle">SN</text><text class="lane-head" x="316" y="-8" text-anchor="middle">SR</text><text class="lane-head" x="532" y="-8" text-anchor="middle">LLR</text><text class="lane-head" x="748" y="-8" text-anchor="middle">TC</text><g class="cell sn" data-id="SN-008" tabindex="0" style="--ring:#ffffff"><title>SN-008 — Gates are honest — a green never hides a skipped check, a stub, or an unmet criterion.</title><rect x="0" y="0.0" width="200" height="17.0" rx="3" fill="#4338ca"></rect><text x="100" y="9.0" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central"><tspan x="100" dy="0">SN-008</tspan></text></g></svg></div><div class="layer" data-layer="archl-sn-009" hidden><svg viewBox="0 -22 848 40" width="848" style="width:100%;max-width:848px;min-width:526px;height:auto" preserveAspectRatio="xMinYMin meet" role="group"><text class="lane-head" x="100" y="-8" text-anchor="middle">SN</text><text class="lane-head" x="316" y="-8" text-anchor="middle">SR</text><text class="lane-head" x="532" y="-8" text-anchor="middle">LLR</text><text class="lane-head" x="748" y="-8" text-anchor="middle">TC</text><g class="cell sn" data-id="SN-009" tabindex="0" style="--ring:#ffffff"><title>SN-009 — A committed secret or private identity is caught before it publishes, in every repo, without extra setup.</title><rect x="0" y="0.0" width="200" height="17.0" rx="3" fill="#4338ca"></rect><text x="100" y="9.0" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central"><tspan x="100" dy="0">SN-009</tspan></text></g></svg></div><div class="layer" data-layer="archl-sn-010" hidden><svg viewBox="0 -22 848 40" width="848" style="width:100%;max-width:848px;min-width:526px;height:auto" preserveAspectRatio="xMinYMin meet" role="group"><text class="lane-head" x="100" y="-8" text-anchor="middle">SN</text><text class="lane-head" x="316" y="-8" text-anchor="middle">SR</text><text class="lane-head" x="532" y="-8" text-anchor="middle">LLR</text><text class="lane-head" x="748" y="-8" text-anchor="middle">TC</text><g class="cell sn" data-id="SN-010" tabindex="0" style="--ring:#ffffff"><title>SN-010 — Documentation stays navigable and honest — links resolve, the vision is declared once, and generated views cannot silently rot.</title><rect x="0" y="0.0" width="200" height="17.0" rx="3" fill="#4338ca"></rect><text x="100" y="9.0" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central"><tspan x="100" dy="0">SN-010</tspan></text></g></svg></div><div class="layer" data-layer="archl-sn-011" hidden><svg viewBox="0 -22 848 40" width="848" style="width:1