ata-node="WI-326" data-label="✓ WI-326" data-summary="A green suite silen…" data-wi="WI-326" data-status="done" style="--ring:#ffffff"><title>WI-326 — A green suite silently hides 47 skipped tests when no POSIX shell is on PATH - make the environment gap ANNOUNCE itself (SN-008: a green never hides a skipped check). Measured 2026-07-26 on Windows: the same tree, the same commit, run twice. With `C:\Program Files\Git\bin` absent from PATH: 1540 passed, 54 skipped. With it present: 1587 passed, 7 skipped, zero failures - so 47 tests were not RUN and nothing said so above the -rs line nobody passes. The 47 are not marginal: 36 are `needs a POSIX shell and git on PATH` in test_pre_commit_hook.py, i.e. the tests guarding the COMMIT FLOOR itself, plus the dev-setup and agent-loop shell paths. Git for Windows ships sh.exe at Git\bin and Git\usr\bin but only puts Git\cmd on PATH, so this is the DEFAULT Windows developer state, not an exotic one - and the handoff&#x27;s recorded &#x27;1579 passed, 7 skipped&#x27; vs a successor&#x27;s &#x27;1540 passed, 54 skipped&#x27; is two sessions reporting incomparable greens without either noticing. Options, cheapest first: (a) a conftest session-header line stating N environment-gated skips and the one PATH entry that would close them; (b) the same, but FAIL the gate tier (check.py) when the count exceeds a declared floor, since a gate bar that skips its own floor tests is the dishonest-green case; (c) have dev-setup.sh --check report it. Prefer (a)+(b): announce always, gate at the gate. Do NOT auto-inject a PATH entry - silently repairing the environment hides the same fact one layer down. (done) · 1</title><rect x="18.0" y="834.0" width="124" height="46" rx="8" fill="#047857" stroke="rgba(15,23,42,.15)"></rect><circle class="port in" cx="18.0" cy="857.0" r="4.5"></circle><circle class="port out" cx="142.0" cy="857.0" r="4.5"></circle><text x="80.0" y="857.0" text-anchor="middle" fill="#fff"><tspan x="80.0" dy="-2" class="blab">✓ W