ce defect to correct rather than a proven end-user failure; confirm against a real screen reader if that is cheap. MECHANIZE (OI-9): ship a structural check on the EMITTED html - no element carrying role=&quot;img&quot; may contain a focusable descendant, and any genuinely non-interactive role=&quot;img&quot; must carry an accessible name. That check owns A2 and would have caught this without a critic. | WI-300 (f) OBLIGATION (2026-07-25 ruling): this row now CLOSES BY BINDING its anchor - land the fix, the test that owns the anchor, AND the child LLR+TC rows naming that test in Evidence, in the SAME commit. A child row cannot land ahead of its test: Draft exempts it from --require-verified but derive_gate returns G0 for a draft, dropping the gate off G3. When the last mechanizable anchor under an SR is bound, retire the coarse LLR/TC and flip that SR to Verification=Test - tests first, flip second, never the reverse. (done) · 3</title><rect x="18.0" y="1310.0" width="124" height="46" rx="8" fill="#047857" stroke="rgba(15,23,42,.15)"></rect><circle class="port in" cx="18.0" cy="1333.0" r="4.5"></circle><circle class="port out" cx="142.0" cy="1333.0" r="4.5"></circle><text x="80.0" y="1333.0" text-anchor="middle" fill="#fff"><tspan x="80.0" dy="-2" class="blab">✓ WI-297</tspan><tspan x="80.0" dy="13" class="bsub">Dashboard SVGs decl…</tspan></text></g><g class="block cancelled" data-tier="work-item" tabindex="0" data-node="WI-298" data-label="⊗ WI-298" data-summary="Dashboard --border …" data-wi="WI-298" data-status="cancelled" style="--ring:#ffffff"><title>WI-298 — Dashboard --border misses the 3:1 graphical-boundary floor in both themes (004-CRITIQUE A4, OPENAI-SOL) - the --border token supplies the boundary for focusable .view regions, detail cards and linked Process-stage rectangles, but measures light #e2e8f0 = 1.23:1 on --surface #ffffff and 1.18:1 on --bg #f8fafc, dark #1e293b = 1.22:1 on --surface #0f172a and 1.29:1 on --bg #0b1120, against the 3:1 floor the 