tyle="--ring:#ffffff"><title>WI-260 — Integrator verdict-gate semantics, owner ruling 2026-07-21 (repo-review-2026-07-21 M-29): unanimous approval - every verdict phase present or required at the exact reviewed head (REVIEW-A, REVIEW-B, and CRITIQUE when the train is render-surface) must have APPROVE as its LATEST verdict before the gate clears; any latest-word CHANGES-REQUESTED blocks, a missing required phase blocks, and an extra approval never substitutes for a missing or dissenting phase. Define the deterministic latest-file-per-phase rule (NNN ordinal at the same sha7) that makes &#x27;&#x27;latest&#x27;&#x27; well-defined (extends the in-train score_reviews.merge_verdict any-dissent-blocks rule the integrator independently verifies, SR-096). Three design decisions MUST be resolved in the WI spec, not silently in the build: (1) required-phase classifier - &#x27;&#x27;required&#x27;&#x27; = the phases the dispatcher actually scheduled for this train (gate and scheduler cannot disagree), with fixture tests for both misclassification directions (scripts-train never deadlocks waiting for an unscheduled CRITIQUE; render-train cannot integrate critique-less, the WI-243 protocol); (2) same-head verdict flips - a later same-sha7 CHANGES-REQUESTED -&gt; APPROVE flip within one phase does NOT silently win (escalate NEEDS-HUMAN or journal loudly; reroll-until-green, L-28 kin), while APPROVE -&gt; CHANGES-REQUESTED is honored; (3) review-policy dial redefinition (owner ruled 2026-07-21): the dial counts REVIEWER phases scheduled (0 = none, 1 = one reviewer, 2 = both), CRITIQUE is orthogonal - required on every render-surface train regardless of dial - and the gate is always unanimity over all scheduled phases (dial 0 render train: critique alone gates; dial 0 non-render train: no verdict phases, integrates on the bar alone - unchanged from today&#x27;&#x27;s required_verdicts=0); a downstream contract change to flag in ADOPTING/resync. Liveness: distinguish phase-dissented