ta-wi="WI-292" data-status="done" style="--ring:#ffffff"><title>WI-292 — Dashboard palette de-collision (117-CRITIQUE U5) - one hue must carry one meaning across the whole document, but four collisions stand: #047857 is both status `done` (status legend, 473 WI fills, and the EXECUTION meter that renders on EVERY tab) and type `Test Case` (icicle TC lane, Knowledge TC block, both legends); #b45309 is both status `active` and type `Process Guide`; phase `1+2` #6d28d9 vs `unphased` #7e22ce sit deltaE 7.4 apart (indistinguishable, rendered side by side in one legend and one roadmap); and --accent #4f46e5 IS the phase-3 accent, so the hover/focus ring painted in --accent VANISHES on exactly the phase-3 block. ROOT CAUSE of the phase pair: WI-247&#x27;s validate_palette.js certified ADJACENT separation (min deltaE 75.6) but the 8-swatch key renders every swatch at once, where PAIRWISE governs (min deltaE 7.4; `2`v`3` 14.7 and `1+2`v`3` 14.8 also miss the &gt;=15 normal-vision target the palette comment itself claims) - a metric gap, not a regression. Fix: declare disjoint palette tokens for status / phase / tier / type, move the colliding hues to non-overlapping families, pick a phase-3 accent distinct from --accent, and validate PAIRWISE (not adjacent) across each rendered key. BLOCKS WI-272: SR-053&#x27;s rubric requires every anchor, so WI-272 cannot earn an APPROVE critique while U5 fails. This is the U5 successor 010-BUILD-DISPOSITION-c67e85b directed the integrator to file. MECHANIZE (OI-9): ship the deterministic checks that own U5 alongside the fix - a cross-vocabulary hex-collision check (no hue may appear in two of STATUS_FILL / TIER_FILL / OKF_TYPE_FILL / PHASE_ACCENTS) and a PAIRWISE deltaE floor across each rendered key (not adjacent-only: that is the exact metric gap that let 7.4 ship). With those tests owning U5, the anchor is a candidate to leave the critique&#x27;s blocking set. | WI-300 (f) OBLIGATION (2026-07-25 ruling): this row now CLOSES BY BINDING 