 explained once CSS tokens are resolved with one open question (sw-node component #44403c, which is not painted as a node fill at all), and A4 already has SIX owning tests so the work is mostly binding plus checking the pair set is closed. Resumption guide with the method, the measurements and the hazards: docs/specs/WI-300-sr052-binding.md. (done) · unphased</title><rect x="18.0" y="1378.0" width="124" height="46" rx="8" fill="#047857" stroke="rgba(15,23,42,.15)"></rect><circle class="port in" cx="18.0" cy="1401.0" r="4.5"></circle><circle class="port out" cx="142.0" cy="1401.0" r="4.5"></circle><text x="80.0" y="1401.0" text-anchor="middle" fill="#fff"><tspan x="80.0" dy="-2" class="blab">✓ WI-313</tspan><tspan x="80.0" dy="13" class="bsub">Bind A1/A3/A4 so SR…</tspan></text></g><g class="block done" data-tier="work-item" tabindex="0" data-node="WI-321" data-label="✓ WI-321" data-summary="A system requiremen…" data-wi="WI-321" data-status="done" style="--ring:#ffffff"><title>WI-321 — A system requirement must be stand-alone: no work-item ids, no process-doc citations in its normative text (owner-raised 2026-07-26 at the first re-attestation sitting). SR-049 had grown `(process.md section 7)` and `(WI-316)` inside its Requirement - provenance a reader cannot resolve without this repo&#x27;s history, in the one row that is supposed to be readable without it. Measured over all 110 SRs before filing: only FIVE rows carry the defect (WI ids in SR-026/049/054/060, a process-doc citation in SR-049), while 65 name a script and 6 name an artifact path - and those are LEGITIMATE, because this kit&#x27;s product IS its scripts, so the name is the system under specification, not a citation. That measurement is what makes a narrow categorical rule affordable instead of a mass edit. SR-049 and SR-054 were cleaned when raised (both already sat in the open Modified window, so the fix cost no new attestation debt); SR-026 and SR-060 are Verified, so cleaning each flips it Modified