.md", "resource": "docs/requirements/interfaces.csv (IF-012)", "title": "IF-012", "type": "Interface"}, "IF-013": {"description": "check.py CLI: --gate G1|G2|G3|all with --tier/--coverage/--lenient runs the active gate's steps as subprocesses and exits nonzero on any required failure (never a silent pass)", "fill": "#701a75", "href": "docs/okf/interfaces/IF-013.md", "resource": "docs/requirements/interfaces.csv (IF-013)", "title": "IF-013", "type": "Interface"}, "IF-014": {"description": "bootstrap.py CLI: --dest DIR [--stack/--domain/--agents/--force] writes the mapped kit files so the scaffold harness runs green; idempotent without --force; stamps docs/kit-version", "fill": "#701a75", "href": "docs/okf/interfaces/IF-014.md", "resource": "docs/requirements/interfaces.csv (IF-014)", "title": "IF-014", "type": "Interface"}, "IF-015": {"description": "agent_loop.py CLI: --wi runs one claimed worker assignment (--train is the optional session tag, defaulting to the branch name), --interactive launches one attached session, --dual-plan runs one decomposition round; a PLAIN launch (no role flag) runs the DRIVE mode (WI-374/WI-381, sibling dispatch.py + lane.py): claim the next ready WI in build order (schedule.py frontier -> integrate.py claim), run a worker session on the claimed branch's worktree, drain the serial merge queue (integrate.py integrate), repeat - re-deriving the frontier every cycle, resuming a parked claim on relaunch, stopping loudly on any composed refusal, never pushing. Preflight refuses broken footing and the per-checkout lock refuses a second coordinator.", "fill": "#701a75", "href": "docs/okf/interfaces/IF-015.md", "resource": "docs/requirements/interfaces.csv (IF-015)", "title": "IF-015", "type": "Interface"}, "IF-016": {"description": "check_vendored.py CLI: network-gated and warn-first; reports a vendored doc copy that has drifted from its recorded upstream source", "fill": "#701a75", "href": "docs/okf/interfaces/IF-016.md", "resource": "docs/r