md", "resource": "docs/requirements/system-requirements.csv (SR-119)", "title": "Superseded: Release on early train end", "type": "System Requirement"}, "SR-120": {"description": "SR-120 is superseded by SR-132 (concurrency-restructure Phase 5, 2026-07-29): the bespoke dispatcher/reservation machinery this specified was deleted outright — git plus the serial local integrator is the integration seam (claims are serial trunk commits, the composed tree is the candidate by construction, recovery is plain git history). Active requirements, implementation links, and decomposition evidence shall cite the replacement row.", "fill": "#0e7490", "href": "docs/okf/system-requirements/SR-120.md", "resource": "docs/requirements/system-requirements.csv (SR-120)", "title": "Superseded: Blocked-constituent disposition", "type": "System Requirement"}, "SR-121": {"description": "SR-121 is superseded by SR-132 (concurrency-restructure Phase 5, 2026-07-29): the bespoke dispatcher/reservation machinery this specified was deleted outright — git plus the serial local integrator is the integration seam (claims are serial trunk commits, the composed tree is the candidate by construction, recovery is plain git history). Active requirements, implementation links, and decomposition evidence shall cite the replacement row.", "fill": "#0e7490", "href": "docs/okf/system-requirements/SR-121.md", "resource": "docs/requirements/system-requirements.csv (SR-121)", "title": "Superseded: Gated downstream migration to the parallel default", "type": "System Requirement"}, "SR-122": {"description": "gen_trajectory.py --check shall fail on stale or missing output, the visible git-derived as-of stamp being excluded from stamp-only comparisons.", "fill": "#0e7490", "href": "docs/okf/system-requirements/SR-122.md", "resource": "docs/requirements/system-requirements.csv (SR-122)", "title": "Dashboard freshness check", "type": "System Requirement"}, "SR-123": {"description": "check_trajectory.py shall warn when a Critique WI closes after CHANGES-REQUESTED without validation evidence changing.", "fill": "#0e7490", "href": "docs/okf/system-requirements/SR-123.md", "resource": "docs/requirements/system-requirements.csv (SR-123)", "title": "Critique closure ratchet", "type": "System Requirement"}, "SR-124": {"description": "schedule.py shall derive a contradiction-safe single-WI scheduling class from PlanMode.", "fill": "#0e7490", "href": "docs/okf/system-requirements/SR-124.md", "resource": "docs/requirements/system-requirements.csv (SR-124)", "title": "Contradiction-safe dual-plan dispatcher class", "type": "System Requirement"}, "SR-125": {"description": "The --dual-plan single-shot round shall map a PAGE through the declared ratification level, hard-gating a human only while the tier in process is still HUMAN-HELD and otherwise reaching the pause-free attention (STALL) end state.", "fill": "#0e7490", "href": "docs/okf/system-requirements/SR-125.md", "resource": "docs/requirements/system-requirements.csv (SR-125)", "title": "PAGE maps through gate policy", "type": "System Requirement"}, "SR-126": {"description": "trace.py shall fail under --strict when any spine row's normative text cites a work item or a process doc.", "fill": "#0e7490", "href": "docs/okf/system-requirements/SR-126.md", "resource": "docs/requirements/system-requirements.csv (SR-126)", "title": "Spine stand-alone rule", "type": "System Requirement"}, "SR-127": {"description": "trace.py shall fail under --strict when a non-Draft requirement repeats its obligation keyword, uses a different modal in normative text, states an obligation with no actor, or uses an unfalsifiable or open-ended term.", "fill": "#0e7490", "href": "docs/okf/system-requirements/SR-127.md", "resource": "docs/requirements/system-requirements.csv (SR-127)", "title": "Requirement form: one testable obligation", "type": "System Requirement"}, "SR-128": {"description": "trace.py shall warn (never fail) when an SR Rationale re-words its own Requirement, or an LLR Detail re-words its parent SR Requirement, past a declared word-overlap threshold.", "fill": "#0e7490", "href": "docs/okf/system-requirements/SR-128.md", "resource": "docs/requirements/system-requirements.csv (SR-128)", "title": "Paraphrase advisory", "type": "System Requirement"}, "SR-129": {"description": "The kit shall provide a mechanical converter between the work-item registry's two homes - the docs/work/ spec folder (status = directory, TOML frontmatter, Deliverable in the body) and the legacy docs/requirements/work-items.csv - refusing any status outside the known vocabulary, any materialization into a non-empty target, and any conversion while an in-flight active/<branch>/ claim exists (conversion is a drained-stop operation), with the round-trip proven over the live registry before an authority flip.", "fill": "#0e7490", "href": "docs/okf/system-requirements/SR-129.md", "resource": "docs/requirements/system-requirements.csv (SR-129)", "title": "Registry representation migration", "type": "System Requirement"}, "SR-130": {"description": "A serial trunk step shall compile docs/log.d/ work-branch log fragments into docs/log.md in merge order derived from git history - validating every fragment before any write, rebasing relative links to the log's home, deleting compiled fragments, failing loudly at the first error and never committing.", "fill": "#0e7490", "href": "docs/okf/system-requirements/SR-130.md", "resource": "docs/requirements/system-requirements.csv (SR-130)", "title": "Serial trunk step compiles log fragments and regenerates authority", "type": "System Requirement"}, "SR-131": {"description": "A tracked docs/work/pause file (TOML: reason, since) shall pause claiming - everything in flight finishes and integrates - read via pause_reason as the ONE pause home (the legacy untracked docs/pause half retired with the dispatcher at Phase 5), failing closed on malformation.", "fill": "#0e7490", "href": "docs/okf/system-requirements/SR-131.md", "resource": "docs/requirements/system-requirements.csv (SR-131)", "title": "Tracked pause drains claiming to a merged stop", "type": "System Requirement"}, "SR-132": {"description": "The local integrator shall claim work via a serial trunk commit (queued spec to docs/work/active/<branch>/, branch cut from that commit, refused while docs/work/pause is present), merge each finished claimed branch --no-ff onto a candidate worktree with the trunk step folded into the merge commit, run the declared bar on the composed tree - refusing on a missing or empty check declaration and on any SKIP in the bar's own report - require the policy-dialed verdict artifacts with git-derived freshness, fast-forward the trunk only on green, and stop loudly on red.", "fill": "#0e7490", "href": "docs/okf/system-requirements/SR-132.md", "resource": "docs/requirements/system-requirements.csv (SR-132)", "title": "Local integrator: serial fail-closed merge queue", "type": "System Requirement"}, "SR-133": {"description": "On a claimed work branch (one whose history holds a docs/work/active/<branch>/ claim) check.py's generated-artifact freshness steps shall SKIP with a stated trunk-lane reason - generated artifacts are trunk-only - while every non-freshness step still runs.", "fill": "#0e7490", "href": "docs/okf/system-requirements/SR-133.md", "resource": "docs/requirements/system-requirements.csv (SR-133)", "title": "Work-branch lane skip for freshness steps", "type": "System Requirement"}, "SR-134": {"description": "The serial trunk step shall regenerate the declared generated artifacts in dependency order - the derived gate before its consumers - failing loudly at the first error and never committing.", "fill": "#0e7490", "href": "docs/okf/system-requirements/SR-134.md", "resource": "docs/requirements/system-requirements.csv (SR-134)", "title": "Trunk step regenerates the declared artifacts in dependency order", "type": "System Requirement"}, "SR-135": {"description": "The generated pending surface shall render a declared pause's since and reason verbatim - no clock - clearing when the pause file is deleted.", "fill": "#0e7490", "href": "docs/okf/system-requirements/SR-135.md", "resource": "docs/requirements/system-requirements.csv (SR-135)", "title": "Pending surface renders the declared pause verbatim", "type": "System Requirement"}, "SR-136": {"description": "check_figures.py shall flag a declared driven figure - a line opting in under the fig: marker convention - that does not carry both the command that produced it and the revision it was driven at, or a derivation naming the declared figures it is computed from, warn-first (exit 0) with --strict gating; presence only, never truth, and an unmarked figure is out of scope by design.", "fill": "#0e7490", "href": "docs/okf/system-requirements/SR-136.md", "resource": "docs/requirements/system-requirements.csv (SR-136)", "title": "Declared-figure provenance", "type": "System Requirement"}, "SR-137": {"description": "The kit shall read every process policy dial from a single `docs/process.toml`, and shall REFUSE — never resolve by precedence — a repo in which any dial is declared both there and in its legacy one-word file. The file's line shape shall be a checked contract: one `key = value` per line under a bare `[section]` header, no dotted keys, no inline tables, no multi-line strings.", "fill": "#0e7490", "href": "docs/okf/system-requirements/SR-137.md", "resource": "docs/requirements/system-requirements.csv (SR-137)", "title": "One policy home, with a checked shape", "type": "System Requirement"}, "SR-138": {"description": "`bootstrap.py --migrate-config` shall fold every legacy one-word policy file into `docs/process.toml` and delete it, and shall NEVER delete a file whose value it did not manage to write. Both bootstrap and the documented re-sync shall run it.", "fill": "#0e7490", "href": "docs/okf/system-requirements/SR-138.md", "resource": "docs/requirements/system-requirements.csv (SR-138)", "title": "Legacy config converts automatically and totally", "type": "System Requirement"}, "SR-139": {"description": "The kit shall express human ratification authority as a cumulative integer 0-4 naming the highest spine tier a human still ratifies, compared against a separately derived SPINE STAGE (0=SN..4=nothing in process) with a declared, auditable mapping to the harness gate. Every unreadable or out-of-range input shall resolve toward MORE human involvement.", "fill": "#0e7490", "href": "docs/okf/system-requirements/SR-139.md", "resource": "docs/requirements/system-requirements.csv (SR-139)", "title": "Ratification as an ordinal over a derived spine stage", "type": "System Requirement"}, "SR-140": {"description": "The kit shall record each acceptance ON THE ACCEPTED ARTIFACT'S OWN ROW - the commit whose tree carries the text that was accepted, and a digest of that row's NORMATIVE cells - never in a second registry keyed on the same artifact; shall report text that has moved away from its recorded anchor regardless of any Status movement; and shall treat an anchor written in the same commit as the text it anchors as an error.", "fill": "#0e7490", "href": "docs/okf/system-requirements/SR-140.md", "resource": "docs/requirements/system-requirements.csv (SR-140)", "title": "The attestation anchor lives on the artifact's own row", "type": "System Requirement"}, "SR-141": {"description": "Admission shall prefer `adjudication` rows over all other ready work, as a stable partition applied at admission rather than by renumbering the ruled rank table, and shall not thereby admit anything past a human-held stop.", "fill": "#0e7490", "href": "docs/okf/system-requirements/SR-141.md", "resource": "docs/requirements/system-requirements.csv (SR-141)", "title": "The loop's priority order is stated and pinned", "type": "System Requirement"}, "SR-142": {"description": "The idle census shall name, as its own class, a test case that is not green while every requirement it verifies is cited by a work item recorded `done`, and shall route it to an ADJUDICATION row whose tier is estimated from measured breadth rather than defaulted.", "fill": "#0e7490", "href": "docs/okf/system-requirements/SR-142.md", "resource": "docs/requirements/system-requirements.csv (SR-142)", "title": "Red test cases under a closed implementation are named and judged", "type": "System Requirement"}, "SR-143": {"description": "The validator shall report, warn-only and never in the exit code, pairs of OPEN work items that overlap by near-identical title, shared requirement citation, or a shared spec of record.", "fill": "#0e7490", "href": "docs/okf/system-requirements/SR-143.md", "resource": "docs/requirements/system-requirements.csv (SR-143)", "title": "Queue overlap is made visible, never blocked", "type": "System Requirement"}, "SR-144": {"description": "A lane that cannot finish shall close into a TERMINAL `partial/` state with one immutable per-close report naming the claimed outcome, the reason, the commit range and the keep/discard split, and shall merge like any other branch. A report declaring neither a split nor an explicit deferral shall be refused, and a second close of the same event shall be refused rather than overwriting the first.", "fill": "#0e7490", "href": "docs/okf/system-requirements/SR-144.md", "resource": "docs/requirements/system-requirements.csv (SR-144)", "title": "Every lane close is a terminal state with an immutable record", "type": "System Requirement"}, "SR-145": {"description": "Every `partial` and `cancelled` close shall earn one disposition row, keyed on the close's own immutable report path; a `complete` close shall be spot-checked at a declared rate rather than gated. Continuing partial work shall mean DRAFTING A SUCCESSOR carrying explicit lineage, never re-opening a terminal row.", "fill": "#0e7490", "href": "docs/okf/system-requirements/SR-145.md", "resource": "docs/requirements/system-requirements.csv (SR-145)", "title": "A lane's outcome is a claim; the adjudicator overrules by minting", "type": "System Requirement"}, "SR-146": {"description": "Every prompt the loop launches shall be a shipped file with strictly filled slots, listed by digest in a freshness-gated generated catalogue, with each session recording which template it used and the fingerprint of what that rendered to.", "fill": "#0e7490", "href": "docs/okf/system-requirements/SR-146.md", "resource": "docs/requirements/system-requirements.csv (SR-146)", "title": "Prompts are reviewable files with a per-session audit trail", "type": "System Requirement"}, "SR-147": {"description": "The kit shall carry the SN->SR->LLR->TC spine in ONE machine-parseable carrier rather than two (stakeholder needs as markdown prose tables, the other three tiers as CSV), and shall provide a mechanical converter that proves the conversion cell-for-cell over the live registries BEFORE the authority flip - refusing, with a nonzero exit that names the row and the field, any conversion in which a cell does not survive the round-trip.", "fill": "#0e7490", "href": "docs/okf/system-requirements/SR-147.md", "resource": "docs/requirements/system-requirements.csv (SR-147)", "title": "One machine-parseable carrier for the requirement spine", "type": "System Requirement"}, "Stakeholder Need": {"description": "29 Stakeholder Need concept(s) — double-click (or focus and press Enter) to descend into them.", "fill": "#4338ca", "href": "", "resource": "", "title": "", "type": "OKF type"}, "System Requirement": {"description": "147 System Requirement concept(s) — double-click (or focus and press Enter) to descend into them.", "fill": "#0e7490", "href": "", "resource": "", "title": "", "type": "OKF type"}, "TC-001": {"description": "Run the trace suite; a linked chain is orphan-free and an injected orphan fails --strict.", "fill": "#0f766e", "href": "docs/okf/test-cases/TC-001.md", "resource": "docs/test/test-cases.csv (TC-001)", "title": "verifies SR-001; LLR-001", "type": "Test Case"}, "TC-002": {"description": "Run the registry-checks suite; duplicate/malformed ids and mis-columned rows fail --strict-integrity.", "fill": "#0f766e", "href": "docs/okf/test-cases/TC-002.md", "resource": "docs/test/test-cases.csv (TC-002)", "title": "verifies SR-002; LLR-002", "type": "Test Case"}, "TC-003": {"description": "Run the registry-checks suite; leftover -000 rows, empty/out-of-vocab fields, and (once the spine is phased) a ratified row whose Phase is not a full-cell bare integer (blank, prefixed like P1/v2, or unparseable) are flagged.", "fill": "#0f766e", "href": "docs/okf/test-cases/TC-003.md", "resource": "docs/test/test-cases.csv (TC-003)", "title": "verifies SR-003; LLR-003", "type": "Test Case"}, "TC-004": {"description": "Run the acceptance-criteria advisory suite; an unpinned comparative warns without changing the exit code.", "fill": "#0f766e", "href": "docs/okf/test-cases/TC-004.md", "resource": "docs/test/test-cases.csv (TC-004)", "title": "verifies SR-004; LLR-004", "type": "Test Case"}, "TC-005": {"description": "Run the off-spine registry suites; PB and current REPO/legacy MOD back-link findings fire and -000 rows are ignored.", "fill": "#0f766e", "href": "docs/okf/test-cases/TC-005.md", "resource": "docs/test/test-cases.csv (TC-005)", "title": "verifies SR-005; LLR-005", "type": "Test Case"}, "TC-006": {"description": "Run the check-harness suite; gate steps run and a missing required tool fails with SKIP(missing).", "fill": "#0f766e", "href": "docs/okf/test-cases/TC-006.md", "resource": "docs/test/test-cases.csv (TC-006)", "title": "verifies SR-006; LLR-006", "type": "Test Case"}, "TC-007": {"description": "Run the stack-profile suite; commands and tiers/coverage/arch-map resolve from stack.ini.", "fill": "#0f766e", "href": "docs/okf/test-cases/TC-007.md", "resource": "docs/test/test-cases.csv (TC-007)", "title": "verifies SR-007; LLR-007", "type": "Test Case"}, "TC-008": {"description": "Run the stack-profile suite; malformed/non-integer/missing-binary profiles fail loudly.", "fill": "#0f766e", "href": "docs/okf/test-cases/TC-008.md", "resource": "docs/test/test-cases.csv (TC-008)", "title": "verifies SR-008; LLR-008", "type": "Test Case"}, "TC-009": {"description": "Run the profile suite; a non-Python profile omits Python-only files and seeds files-mode arch-map.", "fill": "#0f766e", "href": "docs/okf/test-cases/TC-009.md", "resource": "docs/test/test-cases.csv (TC-009)", "title": "verifies SR-009; LLR-009", "type": "Test Case"}, "TC-010": {"description": "Run the bootstrap suite; a fresh scaffold's harness runs green.", "fill": "#0f766e", "href": "docs/okf/test-cases/TC-010.md", "resource": "docs/test/test-cases.csv (TC-010)", "title": "verifies SR-010; LLR-010", "type": "Test Case"}, "TC-011": {"description": "Run the bootstrap suite; a re-run leaves existing files unchanged, --force overwrites, and docs/kit-version is stamped.", "fill": "#0f766e", "href": "docs/okf/test-cases/TC-011.md", "resource": "docs/test/test-cases.csv (TC-011)", "title": "verifies SR-011; LLR-011; SR-111; LLR-121", "type": "Test Case"}, "TC-012": {"description": "Run the check-docs suite; a broken link or missing vision tag fails --stale.", "fill": "#0f766e", "href": "docs/okf/test-cases/TC-012.md", "resource": "docs/test/test-cases.csv (TC-012)", "title": "verifies SR-012; LLR-012", "type": "Test Case"}, "TC-013": {"description": "Run the check-flows suite; a conformant flow passes and a malformed one fails.", "fill": "#0f766e", "href": "docs/okf/test-cases/TC-013.md", "resource": "docs/test/test-cases.csv (TC-013)", "title": "verifies SR-013; LLR-013", "type": "Test Case"}, "TC-014": {"description": "Run the check-perf suite; a within-tolerance metric passes and a regression fails.", "fill": "#0f766e", "href": "docs/okf/test-cases/TC-014.md", "resource": "docs/test/test-cases.csv (TC-014)", "title": "verifies SR-014; LLR-014", "type": "Test Case"}, "TC-015": {"description": "Run the perf-budgets suite; an unresolvable or empty PB Refs is a finding.", "fill": "#0f766e", "href": "docs/okf/test-cases/TC-015.md", "resource": "docs/test/test-cases.csv (TC-015)", "title": "verifies SR-015; LLR-015", "type": "Test Case"}, "TC-016": {"description": "Run the check-stubs suite; a stub at the declared gate fails and clean source passes.", "fill": "#0f766e", "href": "docs/okf/test-cases/TC-016.md", "resource": "docs/test/test-cases.csv (TC-016)", "title": "verifies SR-016; LLR-016", "type": "Test Case"}, "TC-017": {"description": "Run the check-privacy suite; a staged secret is blocked with privacy-check off.", "fill": "#0f766e", "href": "docs/okf/test-cases/TC-017.md", "resource": "docs/test/test-cases.csv (TC-017)", "title": "verifies SR-017; LLR-017", "type": "Test Case"}, "TC-018": {"description": "Run the check-privacy suite; PII/identity classes fire only with privacy-check on and honor EXEMPT_EMAILS.", "fill": "#0f766e", "href": "docs/okf/test-cases/TC-018.md", "resource": "docs/test/test-cases.csv (TC-018)", "title": "verifies SR-018; LLR-018", "type": "Test Case"}, "TC-019": {"description": "Run the pre-commit-hook suite; a failing integrity/secrets check blocks the commit.", "fill": "#0f766e", "href": "docs/okf/test-cases/TC-019.md", "resource": "docs/test/test-cases.csv (TC-019)", "title": "verifies SR-019; LLR-019", "type": "Test Case"}, "TC-020": {"description": "Run the pre-push-hook suite; a secret/identity in the push range blocks the push.", "fill": "#0f766e", "href": "docs/okf/test-cases/TC-020.md", "resource": "docs/test/test-cases.csv (TC-020)", "title": "verifies SR-020; LLR-020", "type": "Test Case"}, "TC-021": {"description": "Run the hook suites' python-probe cases; a missing/aliased python3 reports clearly without crashing.", "fill": "#0f766e", "href": "docs/okf/test-cases/TC-021.md", "resource": "docs/test/test-cases.csv (TC-021)", "title": "verifies SR-021; LLR-021", "type": "Test Case"}, "TC-022": {"description": "Run the check-vendored suite; a