", "resource": "docs/test/test-cases.csv (TC-100)", "title": "verifies SR-109; LLR-097", "type": "Test Case"}, "TC-101": {"description": "Run the check_coverage suite; a module below its floor exits 1 naming it, a declared module absent from the report exits 1, all floors holding exits 0, an absent report SKIPs, an empty census is a no-op, and a malformed floor line fails loudly.", "fill": "#0f766e", "href": "docs/okf/test-cases/TC-101.md", "resource": "docs/test/test-cases.csv (TC-101)", "title": "verifies SR-110; LLR-098", "type": "Test Case"}, "TC-102": {"description": "Generate the dashboard against two fixture registries and assert the SR-089 '>3' rule mechanically: a bundle spanning > 3 OKF types yields the start-collapsed type-tiered drill (know_view returns layers; the Knowledge section renders blocks, not a flat concept graph), a <= 3-type bundle yields None and the flat graph, and the How-SW view collapses above the component threshold on the same rule.", "fill": "#0f766e", "href": "docs/okf/test-cases/TC-102.md", "resource": "docs/test/test-cases.csv (TC-102)", "title": "verifies SR-054; LLR-099", "type": "Test Case"}, "TC-103": {"description": "Generate the dashboard from a tiered fixture registry and assert the drill emits <nav class=\"crumbs\" with a declared data-root-crumb root label, and that the crumb-click handler truncates the trail to the clicked ancestor (trail=trail.slice(0,i+1)) so the parent view is restored.", "fill": "#0f766e", "href": "docs/okf/test-cases/TC-103.md", "resource": "docs/test/test-cases.csv (TC-103)", "title": "verifies SR-054; LLR-100", "type": "Test Case"}, "TC-104": {"description": "Three complementary checks. (1) Unit: _svg_role classifies a native <a href> body, and tabindex in double/single/no quotes, as NOT img, while a static graphic whose text mentions an escaped link stays img. (2) Fixture document walk: generate from a tiered registry and walk every emitted <svg> - an svg declaring role=img must hold no focusable descendant and must carry its own accessible name. (3) Shipped-artifact walk: the same invariant over this repo's own committed PROJECT_STATE.html, which exercises every emitter that actually renders (the loops diagram included) rather than only the two the fixture happens to render. The subtree split strips <script> regions and requires an attributed <svg ...> tag, because embedded JSON prose can contain a literal <svg> that both invents a phantom subtree and swallows a real one.", "fill": "#0f766e", "href": "docs/okf/test-cases/TC-104.md", "resource": "docs/test/test-cases.csv (TC-104)", "title": "verifies SR-052; LLR-101", "type": "Test Case"}, "TC-105": {"description": "Assert the U5 palette-decollision invariants directly against the declared Python constants: (1) TIER_FILL[sn/sr/llr/tc] equals OKF_TYPE_FILL[Stakeholder Need/System Requirement/Low-Level Requirement/Test Case] pairwise (the intentional mirror, checked as a bijection not a set match), (2) no hex is shared across the status / tier+type / sw / phase vocabulary groups outside that mirror, (3) no PHASE_ACCENTS entry equals the light or dark --accent token, (4) pairwise (all C(8,2) pairs) CIE76 deltaE across PHASE_ACCENTS is >= 15.", "fill": "#0f766e", "href": "docs/okf/test-cases/TC-105.md", "resource": "docs/test/test-cases.csv (TC-105)", "title": "verifies SR-053; LLR-102", "type": "Test Case"}, "TC-106": {"description": "Generate the dashboard from a tiered fixture registry and a flat OKF bundle and assert: (1) the drill focus/hl rules and the icicle/flat-DAG/knowledge hl rules all read the SAME --ring custom property (with each emitter's old hue kept only as the CSS fallback); (2) every emitter actually stamps a per-node --ring value inline; (3) the When tab's phase-accent legend emits the shared .legend/<i> markup shape, not the retired span.ph/phaselegend idiom.", "fill": "#0f766e", "href": "docs/okf/test-cases/TC-106.md", "resource": "docs/test/test-cases.csv (TC-106)", "title": "verifies SR-053; LLR-103", "type": "Test Case"}, "TC-107": {"description": "Generate the dashboard with the Process tab enabled (G2 gate) and assert --nhead is declared, .stgt/.stgn resolve to var(--nlabel)/var(--nsub), .hooplab/.hubname resolve to var(--nhead), and none of the four selectors' rule bodies contain a raw px value.", "fill": "#0f766e", "href": "docs/okf/test-cases/TC-107.md", "resource": "docs/test/test-cases.csv (TC-107)", "title": "verifies SR-053; LLR-104", "type": "Test Case"}, "TC-108": {"description": "Two halves, one floor. (a) Compute _ring_ink for every fill declared in STATUS_FILL/TIER_FILL/OKF_TYPE_FILL/SW_NODE_FILL/PHASE_ACCENTS and assert the WCAG contrast ratio against that fill is >= 3, for every fill -- not a hand-picked example. (b) resolve what a browser actually paints for the containment arrow's shaft (.cedge stroke) and marker head (.cedgehead fill) -- mirroring CSS var() fallback against each block's inline --ring and the theme's --accent -- and assert the same >= 3:1 over the same closed fill set in BOTH themes, plus the theme-token (var(--surface)) container fills the fallback still serves; then assert on the RENDERED artifact that every emitted arrow references a marker whose own --ring equals its host block's, since a shaft that passes while a shared head is painted from one hue is precisely the defect.", "fill": "#0f766e", "href": "docs/okf/test-cases/TC-108.md", "resource": "docs/test/test-cases.csv (TC-108)", "title": "verifies SR-054; LLR-105", "type": "Test Case"}, "TC-109": {"description": "Collect every #rrggbb literal declared in gen_trajectory's module-level palette collections (dicts and tuples alike - PHASE_ACCENTS is a tuple, and a dict-only sweep silently under-declares it), then render EVERY emitter and assert each document's hex set is covered by that vocabulary plus the document's own `--token:#hex` theme definitions. Two documented non-concept hexes are allowlisted by name with their reason: --ring's CSS fallback literal, and a retired hex named in the rendered palette-rationale prose (which paints nothing).", "fill": "#0f766e", "href": "docs/okf/test-cases/TC-109.md", "resource": "docs/test/test-cases.csv (TC-109)", "title": "verifies SR-053; LLR-106", "type": "Test Case"}, "TC-110": {"description": "Render every emitter, walk each node group, and assert per node kind: it carries tabindex=\"0\", it carries its role's declared identity/detail attribute, and it carries NEITHER of the other role's attributes. Then assert every declared node kind actually rendered somewhere in the sweep, so the walk cannot degrade into 'the emitters this fixture happened to run'.", "fill": "#0f766e", "href": "docs/okf/test-cases/TC-110.md", "resource": "docs/test/test-cases.csv (TC-110)", "title": "verifies SR-053; LLR-107", "type": "Test Case"}, "TC-113": {"description": "Over the shipped dashboard plus seven fixture renders, collect every focusable element (tabindex=0, button) and role=img graphic with its accessible name (aria-label, else the first child <title>, else text content) and assert: none is empty, none is a bare registry id. Separately assert navigation landmarks in one document carry distinct names.", "fill": "#0f766e", "href": "docs/okf/test-cases/TC-113.md", "resource": "docs/test/test-cases.csv (TC-113)", "title": "verifies SR-052; LLR-108", "type": "Test Case"}, "TC-114": {"description": "Enumerate every declared colour vocabulary and compute pairwise CIE76 deltaE over all cross pairs, skipping the declared tier<->okf mirror (and asserting that mirrored pair is byte-equal). Assert >= 15 within a vocabulary and >= 12 across. Pure constant arithmetic - no fixture render needed.", "fill": "#0f766e", "href": "docs/okf/test-cases/TC-114.md", "resource": "docs/test/test-cases.csv (TC-114)", "title": "verifies SR-053; LLR-109", "type": "Test Case"}, "TC-115": {"description": "Over the shipped dashboard plus seven fixture renders, assert each declared --w-*/--o-*/--r-* token is defined exactly once, and that every stroke-width, opacity, stroke-opacity and border-radius appearing in a PAINT surface (style block or style attribute) resolves to one of them. Separately assert the SVG rx literals in the emitter source, and the rx values in every render, are a subset of SVG_RX.", "fill": "#0f766e", "href": "docs/okf/test-cases/TC-115.md", "resource": "docs/test/test-cases.csv (TC-115)", "title": "verifies SR-053; LLR-110", "type": "Test Case"}, "TC-116": {"description": "Over the shipped dashboard plus seven fixture renders, assert each declared scale step is defined exactly once and that every font-size in a PAINT surface resolves to a declared step - never a raw literal, never a token from another scale. Paint surfaces only, because the rendered document also QUOTES CSS in prose and a whole-document scan judges documentation as code. Also caps the declared set, so a scale cannot grow a step per call site.", "fill": "#0f766e", "href": "docs/okf/test-cases/TC-116.md", "resource": "docs/test/test-cases.csv (TC-116)", "title": "verifies SR-053; LLR-111", "type": "Test Case"}, "TC-117": {"description": "Over the shipped dashboard plus seven fixture renders: derive every querySelectorAll selector from the document's own scripts and assert each is classified control-or-not; for every control selector, match its elements in the script-stripped markup (quote-aware tag scan; the tiny selector grammar is matched exactly and anything richer fails loudly) and assert each match is focusable (tabindex=0, a button, or a link with href); assert every classified selector is seen somewhere and every control selector matches at least one element (non-vacuous both ways). Separately assert the only emitted tabindex values are 0 and -1, with -1 confined to roving tablist buttons.", "fill": "#0f766e", "href": "docs/okf/test-cases/TC-117.md", "resource": "docs/test/test-cases.csv (TC-117)", "title": "verifies SR-052; LLR-112", "type": "Test Case"}, "TC-118": {"description": "Over the shipped dashboard plus seven fixture renders: resolve the document's token definitions, collect every legend swatch carrying a non-empty word label (var() resolved), collect every vocabulary member painted in a PAINT surface of the script-stripped markup (style blocks, style attributes, fill/stroke attributes), and assert each painted member's hex appears as a worded swatch in the SAME document; assert every vocabulary is exercised somewhere in the sweep. Plus the tier-legend bijection: the icicle legend's swatch list equals TIER_FILL in declaration order.", "fill": "#0f766e", "href": "docs/okf/test-cases/TC-118.md", "resource": "docs/test/test-cases.csv (TC-118)", "title": "verifies SR-052; LLR-113", "type": "Test Case"}, "TC-119": {"description": "Reflect every UPPERCASE module-level constant RECURSIVELY (nested dicts/tuples/sets and bare strings) for any 3/4/6/8-digit hex member and assert the hex-bearing set is exactly the five declared vocabularies, every member canonical 6-digit lowercase, and every member clearing 4.5:1 against its label ink (white, or the declared queued dark-ink exception) and 3:1 for its computed _ring_ink. Separately derive every fill:var() token from the emitted CSS and assert each carries a declared role, with white-text-fill roles clearing 4.5:1 under white and container-fill roles keeping --text readable, in BOTH themes. The six sibling A4 tests keep owning their specific arithmetic and are cited as evidence beside the closure.", "fill": "#0f766e", "href": "docs/okf/test-cases/TC-119.md", "resource": "docs/test/test-cases.csv (TC-119)", "title": "verifies SR-052; LLR-114", "type": "Test Case"}, "TC-120": {"description": "Generate the dashboard from a zero-active/all-queued fixture — the condition under which a next-work surface can exist in the emitter and render nothing plus a committed module map, then resolve each of the three core reading tasks' entry points from the emitted document and assert each is LABELLED and reachable in <= 1 tab switch: the landing Definition-completeness/Execution cards (task 1, 0 switches), the landing Next-work card (task 2, 0 switches), and the How-SW nav tab (task 3, 1 switch). Assert the next-work surface renders NAMED content (not an empty region) on the zero-active artifact; its non-emptiness across the waiting-with-predecessor and drained fixtures is owned by the next-work tests named in this row's Evidence.", "fill": "#0f766e", "href": "docs/okf/test-cases/TC-120.md", "resource": "docs/test/test-cases.csv (TC-120)", "title": "verifies SR-054; LLR-115", "type": "Test Case"}, "TC-121": {"description": "Generate the dashboard and derive EVERY emitted <svg> from the document (not a hand list, so a fourth emitter cannot skip the rule); assert each carries the responsive style and none keeps a bare fixed width; assert the emitted min/max ratio equals the declared SHRINK_FLOOR constant.", "fill": "#0f766e", "href": "docs/okf/test-cases/TC-121.md", "resource": "docs/test/test-cases.csv (TC-121)", "title": "verifies SR-054; LLR-116", "type": "Test Case"}, "TC-122": {"description": "Sweep EVERY emitter document (the shipped artifact plus a fixture per emitter, the A2-review rule that a walk judges only what its fixture renders) and, per document: derive the theme-varying/-invariant token families from the emitted CSS; assert exactly one prefers-color-scheme block and one color-scheme declaration, both at :root; assert body's own background and ink are theme-varying; assert no CSS rule pairs a background and an ink from two families; assert no emitted SVG node pairs an inline rect fill with an inline text fill from two families. Then, accumulated ACROSS the sweep (because one document cannot distinguish -paints on the page background- from -this emitter does not render those nodes-), assert every CSS-declared SVG text fill matches the family its host nodes actually paint, or is theme-varying when it has no host anywhere.", "fill": "#0f766e", "href": "docs/okf/test-cases/TC-122.md", "resource": "docs/test/test-cases.csv (TC-122)", "title": "verifies SR-054; LLR-117", "type": "Test Case"}, "TC-123": {"description": "Drive gen_open_items over temp repos: assert a pending registry row renders as a brief and a RULED row does not; that Draft AND Modified spine rows both surface (ratification owed vs re-attest owed) while a Verified row does not; that a section with no changed cells says CHECK THE BASELINE and never nothing-changed; that --check bites on drift, MASKS the machine-local region (and still bites outside it), and re-reads the baseline stamp the file declares; that the whole thing is vacuous with neither registry nor view; that registry prose is HTML-escaped; that the word diff marks only what moved and the percentage counts words not whitespace; and that the theme tokens equal the dashboard's emitted values (a drift guard, not an extraction).", "fill": "#0f766e", "href": "docs/okf/test-cases/TC-123.md", "resource": "docs/test/test-cases.csv (TC-123)", "title": "verifies SR-049; LLR-118", "type": "Test Case"}, "TC-124": {"description": "Generate the dashboard over a tiered fixture carrying one sentence-length stakeholder need (the shape that overflowed), then sweep EVERY drill block in the emitted document - not a per-view list, because the defect lives in the one shared label emitter that feeds four views. For each block, take its rect and each label line's own x/dy from the markup, measure the line's ink with the emitter's declared per-character widths and the font sizes the emitted CSS declares (unescaping entities first, so an apostrophe is one glyph and not six), and assert the ink box lies inside the rect on both axes. Assert the sentence-length need is actually among the swept labels, so the sweep cannot pass vacuously; separately assert the fit path itself (a second line broken on a word, then an ellipsis, with the full string still reachable) and that a sub-label which already fits keeps the untouched two-line grid. Second half: render the next-work card from a fixture carrying the 109-character _NW_LONG clause and assert it appears WHOLE with no ellipsis in the list, the fixture asserted longer than the retired 60-character budget so the check cannot pass vacuously; then, from a fixture past the declared bound, assert a native details/summary with a visible cue, that the emitted head and remainder rejoin to exactly the clause and the cut fell on a word, and that the reveal is neither script-dependent nor hidden by the emitter's own CSS.", "fill": "#0f766e", "href": "docs/okf/test-cases/TC-124.md", "resource": "docs/test/test-cases.csv (TC-124)", "title": "verifies SR-054; LLR-119", "type": "Test Case"}, "TC-125": {"description": "Sweep the union of emitter documents (the shipped PROJECT_STATE.html plus a fixture per emitter - the A2-review rule that a walk judges only what its fixture renders) and, per emitted <svg>: parse every node's id and rect and every wire's path data, sample each path into the polyline the router's own hit-test uses (so the test and the emitter describe one curve), drop the rects whose own port circle holds an endpoint, and assert the polyline crosses none of the rest. Assert the sweep found wires at all AND that at least one of them is a DETOUR, so a broken router cannot pass a sweep in which nothing needed re-routing.", "fill": "#0f766e", "href": "docs/okf/test-cases/TC-125.md", "resource": "docs/test/test-cases.csv (TC-125)", "title": "verifies SR-054; LLR-120", "type": "Test Case"}, "TC-126": {"description": "Run the spine stand-alone suite; a WI id or process-doc citation in a normative cell of any spine registry is a finding, and a script name, artifact path, rubric or sibling id is not.", "fill": "#0f766e", "href": "docs/okf/test-cases/TC-126.md", "resource": "docs/test/test-cases.csv (TC-126)", "title": "verifies SR-126; LLR-133", "type": "Test Case"}, "TC-127": {"description": "Run the requirement-form suite; each of the six rules fires on its own defect shape, and the negative half (Draft, zero-`shall`, `must`, a multi-clause AcceptanceCriteria, a passive with a named actor) does not.", "fill": "#0f766e", "href": "docs/okf/test-cases/TC-127.md", "resource": "docs/test/test-cases.csv (TC-127)", "title": "verifies SR-127; LLR-134", "type": "Test Case"}, "TC-128": {"description": "Run the paraphrase-advisory suite; an echoing child warns while a real decomposition naming module and mechanism does not, and the exit code is unchanged either way.", "fill": "#0f766e", "href": "docs/okf/test-cases/TC-128.md", "resource": "docs/test/test-cases.csv (TC-128)", "title": "verifies SR-128; LLR-135", "type": "Test Case"}, "TC-129": {"description": "Run the converter suite: the live registry round-trips in whichever home is authoritative; an unknown status is refused by name; a corrupted rebuilt spec reds the cell comparison after a clean-first control; folder->CSV->folder is parse-equal including a hand-filed spec.", "fill": "#0f766e", "href": "docs/okf/test-cases/TC-129.md", "resource": "docs/test/test-cases.csv (TC-129)", "title": "verifies SR-129; LLR-136", "type": "Test Case"}, "TC-130": {"description": "Run the trunk-step suite: committed fragments compile in git order with links rebased and fragments deleted; an uncommitted, heading-less or reserved-heading fragment blocks the whole batch; a fragment-free run is a clean idempotent no-op.", "fill": "#0f766e", "href": "docs/okf/test-cases/TC-130.md", "resource": "docs/test/test-cases.csv (TC-130)", "title": "verifies SR-130; LLR-137", "type": "Test Case"}, "TC-131": {"description": "Run the pause suites: the tracked home pauses via pause_reason with the unchanged return contract; a stray legacy file is inert; malformation pauses fail-closed with the pinned loud placeholder.", "fill": "#0f766e", "href": "docs/okf/test-cases/TC-131.md", "resource": "docs/test/test-cases.csv (TC-131)", "title": "verifies SR-131; LLR-138", "type": "Test Case"}, "TC-132": {"description": "Run the integrator suite: each claim refusal fires by name and the green claim moves the spec and cuts the branch; finished-branch detection keys on the tree; the verdict gate refuses absent, CHANGES-REQUESTED and stale-APPROVE verdicts and passes a fresh APPROVE; a missing or empty bar declaration refuses; the window audit flags a non-merge product commit and passes a bookkeeping-only window; one end-to-end claim->work->close->integrate run fast-forwards the trunk to a --no-ff merge commit.", "fill": "#0f766e", "href": "docs/okf/test-cases/TC-132.md", "resource": "docs/test/test-cases.csv (TC-132)", "title": "verifies SR-132; LLR-140", "type": "Test Case"}, "TC-133": {"description": "Inspect the fifteen Phase-5 legacy SR rows, their SupersededBy links to SR-132, and the post-deletion registries.", "fill": "#0f766e", "href": "docs/okf/test-cases/TC-133.md", "resource": "docs/test/test-cases.csv (TC-133)", "title": "verifies SR-061; SR-062; SR-065; SR-095; SR-096; SR-097; SR-098; SR-099; SR-100; SR-101; SR-117; SR-118; SR-119; SR-120; SR-121", "type": "Test Case"}, "TC-134": {"description": "Run the check-harness lane suite: a claimed work branch skips the declared freshness steps with the §5.2 notice and untouched exit code while non-freshness steps still run; the closing commit and its successors keep the skip (history-derived signal); the trunk lane never skips.", "fill": "#0f766e", "href": "docs/okf/test-cases/TC-134.md", "resource": "docs/test/test-cases.csv (TC-134)", "title": "verifies SR-133; LLR-141", "type": "Test Case"}, "TC-135": {"description": "Run the trunk-step regen suite: --regen skips absent artifact families with a notice and stops loudly at the first failing generator, regenerating in dependency order.", "fill": "#0f766e", "href": "docs/okf/test-cases/TC-135.md", "resource": "docs/test/test-cases.csv (TC-135)", "title": "verifies SR-134; LLR-142", "type": "Test Case"}, "TC-136": {"description": "Run the pending-surface pause suite: the block renders since/reason verbatim (no clock), omits the stamp when since is empty, matches the reader's fail-closed placeholder on malformation, clears on deletion, and is deterministic.", "fill": "#0f766e", "href": "docs/okf/test-cases/TC-136.md", "resource": "docs/test/test-cases.csv (TC-136)", "title": "verifies SR-135; LLR-139", "type": "Test Case"}, "TC-137": {"description": "Run the drive suite: an unwired agent command refuses before any claim while an empty queue still drains to exit 0; a refusing claim rung, a stranded claim, a dirty trunk and a red composed-tree bar each stop the run by name; the tracked pause appearing mid-run stops the next cycle at exit 8; NEEDS-HUMAN propagates at exit 7 with the claim parked; a DONE-reporting worker that finishes nothing trips the stall guard; and two end-to-end runs against the real bar prove the green path (claim->build->merge->drained banner) and the red path (candidate parked, claim intact). The plain agent_loop.py launch enters the drive mode as a subprocess.", "fill": "#0f766e", "href": "docs/okf/test-cases/TC-137.md", "resource": "docs/test/test-cases.csv (TC-137)", "title": "verifies SR-026; LLR-143", "type": "Test Case"}, "TC-138": {"description": "Run the handback suite: a partial close moves each claimed spec to the terminal partial/ and writes its immutable per-close report under docs/handbacks/, leaves the branch finished, is CLEAN under the real trajectory check (R-A exempts partial — the spec's definition is deliberately byte-identical), refuses a second close without residue, and is LOUD when a terminal spec has no report; an already-declared blockref and an existing Deliverable survive; a branch trunk holds no claim for is refused. The quarantine arm reverts the product paths and keeps the failing diff as a bar-inert .patch, reverts a RENAME correctly (the --name-status -z stream read as records, not pairs - mutation-proven), leaves the handback bookkeeping alone, refuses when the red is not the lane's