test-cases/TC-144.md", "resource": "docs/test/test-cases.csv (TC-144)", "title": "verifies SR-132; LLR-150", "type": "Test Case"}, "TC-145": {"description": "Run the integrator claim suite: a spine claim succeeds on an idle station (the deleted safety-class arm, red-then-green); a hand claim while another holder has the dispatch lock refuses naming the lock and leaves the queue untouched, while dispatch_lock_held=True proceeds; a spine batch claims as ONE bookkeeping commit whose subject joins the ids and whose specs all land in active/<branch>/; every pre-existing single-WI claim contract (abandoned-claim re-cut, relink oracle, minted-id rung, RULING-6 audit) holds unchanged.", "fill": "#0f766e", "href": "docs/okf/test-cases/TC-145.md", "resource": "docs/test/test-cases.csv (TC-145)", "title": "verifies SR-132; LLR-151", "type": "Test Case"}, "TC-146": {"description": "Run the schedule + integrate suites' adjudication cases: the kind classifies exclusive at rank 1 (the reserved slot, pinned by name); an adjudication-only lane's refresh runs NO bar yet still commits a verified Bar-Green attestation whose summary says no-bar, while a mixed batch bars as usual (fail toward the bar); bar = G2 reaches check.py as --gate G2 (asserted off the recording stub's own argv), an undeclared bar passes no --gate, and a malformed value refuses the refresh naming it.", "fill": "#0f766e", "href": "docs/okf/test-cases/TC-146.md", "resource": "docs/test/test-cases.csv (TC-146)", "title": "verifies SR-093; LLR-152", "type": "Test Case"}, "TC-147": {"description": "Run the intake suite against real git repos, red-then-green per trigger (trigger (b) keys on the close's immutable REPORT PATH, so a re-sweep dedupes exactly and a genuinely second close is a second row): a ratified SR amendment mints ONE adjudication row (id max+1, blockref empty, the before/after listing in ## Context) and an LLR SR-Refs re-point mints while a Module-only move stays silent (the ruled routing); a merged hand