ery declared coverage gap warns without failing and each suppression/vacuity case stays silent.", "meta": "Method: Run endpoint/direction, source-sink, Active-citation, Contracts, opt-out, and strict non-gating coverage cases.", "status": "Verified"}, "TC-081": {"tier": "tc", "title": "verifies SR-075;LLR-080", "body": "Seams render as labeled edges in both views; absent seams retain fallback; output is deterministic.", "meta": "Method: Generate dashboard and architecture views with and without declared seams.", "status": "Verified"}, "TC-082": {"tier": "tc", "title": "verifies SR-080;LLR-045", "body": "Managed scheduling matches policy with redacted logged routing; bad prompts fail preflight; unmanaged mode stays legacy.", "meta": "Method: Run review-policy 0/1/2, prompt-map, redaction, selection logging, verdict, and unmanaged cases.", "status": "Verified"}, "TC-083": {"tier": "tc", "title": "verifies SR-081;LLR-046", "body": "Scores and decay match fixtures; all tripwires fire as gates; length is never positive; persistence is stable.", "meta": "Method: Run substance components, corroboration, tripwires, decay, verdict parsing, and CLI cases.", "status": "Verified"}, "TC-084": {"tier": "tc", "title": "verifies SR-082;LLR-081", "body": "The fixed win-stay/lose-shift sequence and every paging condition match policy.", "meta": "Method: Drive swap, tier-up, shared failure, contradiction, tripwire, and the ratification-level escalation branches (all four human_held x keep_nondependent cells).", "status": "Modified"}, "TC-085": {"tier": "tc", "title": "verifies SR-085;LLR-082", "body": "CHANGES-REQUESTED reworks within the bound and cap exhaustion pages through policy.", "meta": "Method: Run critique approval, rework, configured-cap exhaustion, and the ratification-level disposition cases.", "status": "Modified"}, "TC-086": {"tier": "tc", "title": "verifies SR-086;LLR-083;SR-123;LLR-084", "body": "Satisfies SR-086 and SR-123 AcceptanceCriteria", "meta": "Method: Run Critique vocabulary/LLR-completeness and staged closure-ratchet cases.", "status": "Verified"}, "TC-087": {"tier": "tc", "title": "verifies SR-088;LLR-085", "body": "Contained views nest and deduplicate crossing seams; no containment stays byte-identical and deterministic.", "meta": "Method: Generate nested/flat How-SW containment and boundary aggregation cases.", "status": "Verified"}, "TC-088": {"tier": "tc", "title": "verifies SR-090;LLR-086", "body": "Containment creates bounded component tiers that descend to modules; uncontained input remains flat.", "meta": "Method: Run component-to-module How-SW tier and top-width-bound cases.", "status": "Verified"}, "TC-089": {"tier": "tc", "title": "verifies SR-091;LLR-087", "body": "Visible endpoints use input/output ports and crossing seams aggregate without duplicates.", "meta": "Method: Render seams at hierarchy ports and crossing container boundaries.", "status": "Verified"}, "TC-090": {"tier": "tc", "title": "verifies SR-092;LLR-088", "body": "Each input descends one layer and breadcrumb restores the parent in the self-contained render.", "meta": "Method: Exercise pointer/keyboard descent and breadcrumb restoration.", "status": "Verified"}, "TC-091": {"tier": "tc", "title": "verifies SR-094;LLR-089", "body": "Only invalid rows fail closed with reason codes and disjoint valid rows remain schedulable.", "meta": "Method: Classify missing, unknown, structurally contradictory, critique, checkpoint, and dual-plan WIs beside disjoint valid work.", "status": "Verified"}, "TC-097": {"tier": "tc", "title": "verifies SR-107;LLR-095;SR-124;LLR-131", "body": "Satisfies SR-107 and SR-124 AcceptanceCriteria", "meta": "Method: Run direct worker/flag refusal and PlanMode-derived classification/contradiction cases.", "status": "Verified"}, "TC-098": {"tier": "tc", "title": "verifies SR-108;LLR-096;SR-125;LLR-132", "body": "Satisfies SR-108 and SR-125 AcceptanceCriteria", "meta": "Method: Run dispatcher SELECT, human-held PAGE, loop-held PAGE continuation, regeneration failure, and salvage cases, plus the dual-plan PAGE on a human-held tier, on a loop-held tier, and with keep_nondependent, at both the dispatcher and the --dual-plan single-shot entry.", "status": "Modified"}, "TC-099": {"tier": "tc", "title": "verifies SR-037;SR-038;SR-044;SR-045;SR-047;SR-048;SR-051;SR-058;SR-063;SR-064;SR-066", "body": "All frozen links resolve and are acyclic; no legacy row retains an LLR; this TC cites every legacy row.", "meta": "Method: Inspect the eleven legacy SR rows, their SupersededBy graph, replacement targets, and post-split LLR parents.", "status": "Verified"}, "TC-100": {"tier": "tc", "title": "verifies SR-109;LLR-097", "body": "Done-with-SpecRef and orphan-spec cases WARN plain (exit 0) and fail --strict (exit 1); the deferred-cited doc and README/-000 files stay clean under --strict.", "meta": "Method: Run check_trajectory over registries with a done+SpecRef row, an uncited live spec, a deferred-cited shared doc, and scaffold boilerplate.", "status": "Verified"}, "TC-101": {"tier": "tc", "title": "verifies SR-110;LLR-098", "body": "Satisfies SR-110 AcceptanceCriteria", "meta": "Method: Run the check_coverage suite; a module below its floor exits 1 naming it, a declared module absent from the report exits 1, all floors holding exits 0, an absent report SKIPs, an empty census is a no-op, and a malformed floor line fails loudly.", "status": "Verified"}, "TC-102": {"tier": "tc", "title": "verifies SR-054;LLR-099", "body": "Above the threshold the view is start-collapsed; at or below it renders flat. Both directions asserted. This widens to the landing What icicle: above 3 SNs it is a start-collapsed SN drill with NO leaf cell in the opening layer; at or below 3 it stays flat and byte-identical.", "meta": "Method: Generate the dashboard against two fixture registries and assert the SR-089 '>3' rule mechanically: a bundle spanning > 3 OKF types yields the start-collapsed type-tiered drill (know_view returns layers; the Knowledge section renders blocks, not a flat concept graph), a <= 3-type bundle yields None and the flat graph, and the How-SW view collapses above the component threshold on the same rule.", "status": "Verified"}, "TC-103": {"tier": "tc", "title": "verifies SR-054;LLR-100", "body": "Breadcrumb nav present with a root crumb; crumb click restores the ancestor view.", "meta": "Method: Generate the dashboard from a tiered fixture registry and assert the drill emits <nav class=\"crumbs\" with a declared data-root-crumb root label, and that the crumb-click handler truncates the trail to the clicked ancestor (trail=trail.slice(0,i+1)) so the parent view is restored.", "status": "Verified"}, "TC-104": {"tier": "tc", "title": "verifies SR-052;LLR-101", "body": "On the shipped artifact: 44 svg containers, 0 role=img, 0 focusable descendants inside a children-presentational subtree, 1171 focusables total (non-vacuous). Asserts NOT-children-presentational rather than role=group specifically, so dropping the role or using graphics-document would also pass - the test must not pin an implementation LLR-101 leaves open.", "meta": "Method: Three complementary checks. (1) Unit: _svg_role classifies a native <a href> body, and tabindex in double/single/no quotes, as NOT img, while a static graphic whose text mentions an escaped link stays img. (2) Fixture document walk: generate from a tiered registry and walk every emitted <svg> - an svg declaring role=img must hold no focusable descendant and must carry its own accessible name. (3) Shipped-artifact walk: the same invariant over this repo's own committed PROJECT_STATE.html, which exercises every emitter that actually renders (the loops diagram included) rather than only the two the fixture happens to render. The subtree split strips <script> regions and requires an attributed <svg ...> tag, because embedded JSON prose can contain a literal <svg> that both invents a phantom subtree and swallows a real one.", "status": "Verified"}, "TC-105": {"tier": "tc", "title": "verifies SR-053;LLR-102", "body": "No cross-vocabulary hex collision found; no phase equals --accent; minimum pairwise deltaE >= 15 (achieved 18.1).", "meta": "Method: Assert the U5 palette-decollision invariants directly against the declared Python constants: (1) TIER_FILL[sn/sr/llr/tc] equals OKF_TYPE_FILL[Stakeholder Need/System Requirement/Low-Level Requirement/Test Case] pairwise (the intentional mirror, checked as a bijection not a set match), (2) no hex is shared across the status / tier+type / sw / phase vocabulary groups outside that mirror, (3) no PHASE_ACCENTS entry equals the light or dark --accent token, (4) pairwise (all C(8,2) pairs) CIE76 deltaE across PHASE_ACCENTS is >= 15.", "status": "Verified"}, "TC-106": {"tier": "tc", "title": "verifies SR-053;LLR-103", "body": "Ring token and legend markup identical in shape across every emitter; no retired span.ph/phaselegend selector remains.", "meta": "Method: Generate the dashboard from a tiered fixture registry and a flat OKF bundle and assert: (1) the drill focus/hl rules and the icicle/flat-DAG/knowledge hl rules all read the SAME --ring custom property (with each emitter's old hue kept only as the CSS fallback); (2) every emitter actually stamps a per-node --ring value inline; (3) the When tab's phase-accent legend emits the shared .legend/<i> markup shape, not the retired span.ph/phaselegend idiom.", "status": "Verified"}, "TC-107": {"tier": "tc", "title": "verifies SR-053;LLR-104", "body": "No ad-hoc px font-size remains on .stgt/.stgn/.hooplab/.hubname; all four resolve to a declared CSS custom property.", "meta": "Method: Generate the dashboard with the Process tab enabled (G2 gate) and assert --nhead is declared, .stgt/.stgn resolve to var(--nlabel)/var(--nsub), .hooplab/.hubname resolve to var(--nhead), and none of the four selectors' rule bodies contain a raw px value.", "status": "Verified"}, "TC-108": {"tier": "tc", "title": "verifies SR-054;LLR-105", "body": "Every declared fill clears >= 3:1 against its computed ring ink; worst case observed ~4.58:1. Half (b) was proven against the pre-fix code first, failing at the critique's measured 1.0596:1 (#4f46e5 on #0369a1).", "meta": "Method: Two halves, one floor. (a) Compute _ring_ink for every fill declared in STATUS_FILL/TIER_FILL/OKF_TYPE_FILL/SW_NODE_FILL/PHASE_ACCENTS and assert the WCAG contrast ratio against that fill is >= 3, for every fill -- not a hand-picked example. (b) resolve what a browser actually paints for the containment arrow's shaft (.cedge stroke) and marker head (.cedgehead fill) -- mirroring CSS var() fallback against each block's inline --ring and the theme's --accent -- and assert the same >= 3:1 over the same closed fill set in BOTH themes, plus the theme-token (var(--surface)) container fills the fallback still serves; then assert on the RENDERED artifact that every emitted arrow references a marker whose own --ring equals its host block's, since a shaft that passes while a shared head is painted from one hue is precisely the defect.", "status": "Verified"}, "TC-109": {"tier": "tc", "title": "verifies SR-053;LLR-106", "body": "Every hex in every rendered document resolves to a declared vocabulary member or a theme token; no emitter paints a concept with a literal.", "meta": "Method: Collect every #rrggbb literal declared in gen_trajectory's module-level palette collections (dicts and tuples alike - PHASE_ACCENTS is a tuple, and a dict-only sweep silently under-declares it), then render EVERY emitter and assert each document's hex set is covered by that vocabulary plus the document's own `--token:#hex` theme definitions. Two documented non-concept hexes are allowlisted by name with their reason: --ring's CSS fallback literal, and a retired hex named in the rendered palette-rationale prose (which paints nothing).", "status": "Verified"}, "TC-110": {"tier": "tc", "title": "verifies SR-053;LLR-107", "body": "All four node kinds render; every node is focusable the shared way and addressed through exactly one declared attribute vocabulary.", "meta": "Method: Render every emitter, walk each node group, and assert per node kind: it carries tabindex=\"0\", it carries its role's declared identity/detail attribute, and it carries NEITHER of the other role's attributes. Then assert every declared node kind actually rendered somewhere in the sweep, so the walk cannot degrade into 'the emitters this fixture happened to run'.", "status": "Verified"}, "TC-113": {"tier": "tc", "title": "verifies SR-052;LLR-108", "body": "Every control is named, no name is a bare id, and no two navigation landmarks share a name.", "meta": "Method: Over the shipped dashboard plus seven fixture renders, collect every focusable element (tabindex=0, button) and role=img graphic with its accessible name (aria-label, else the first child <title>, else text content) and assert: none is empty, none is a bare registry id. Separately assert navigation landmarks in one document carry distinct names.", "status": "Verified"}, "TC-114": {"tier": "tc", "title": "verifies SR-053;LLR-109", "body": "No pair below its floor; closest surviving pair 12.5 (Process Guide vs phase[2]).", "meta": "Method: Enumerate every declared colour vocabulary and compute pairwise CIE76 deltaE over all cross pairs, skipping the declared tier<->okf mirror (and asserting that mirrored pair is byte-equal). Assert >= 15 within a vocabulary and >= 12 across. Pure constant arithmetic - no fixture render needed.", "status": "Verified"}, "TC-115": {"tier": "tc", "title": "verifies SR-053;LLR-110", "body": "No raw weight/alpha/corner literal and no undeclared rx value survives.", "meta": "Method: Over the shipped dashboard plus seven fixture renders, assert each declared --w-*/--o-*/--r-* token is defined exactly once, and that every stroke-width, opacity, stroke-opacity and border-radius appearing in a PAINT surface (style block or style attribute) resolves to one of them. Separately assert the SVG rx literals in the emitter source, and the rx values in every render, are a subset of SVG_RX.", "status": "Verified"}, "TC-116": {"tier": "tc", "title": "verifies SR-053;LLR-111", "body": "Zero raw font-size literals; every size names a declared step.", "meta": "Method: Over the shipped dashboard plus seven fixture renders, assert each declared scale step is defined exactly once and that every font-size in a PAINT surface resolves to a declared step - never a raw literal, never a token from another scale. Paint surfaces only, because the rendered document also QUOTES CSS in prose and a whole-document scan judges documentation as code. Also caps the declared set, so a scale cannot grow a step per call site.", "status": "Verified"}, "TC-117": {"tier": "tc", "title": "verifies SR-052;LLR-112", "body": "Every wired control is keyboard-focusable; no unclassified, stale, or non-literal selector; no positive tabindex; every control wiring loop that attaches click/dblclick attaches focus or keydown beside it. Verified to fail against a control losing its tabindex, a newly wired selector (single- AND double-quoted), a positive tabindex, and a wiring loop stripped of its focus path.", "meta": "Method: Over the shipped dashboard plus seven fixture renders: derive every querySelectorAll selector from the document's own scripts and assert each is classified control-or-not; for every control selector, match its elements in the script-stripped markup (quote-aware tag scan; the tiny selector grammar is matched exactly and anything richer fails loudly) and assert each match is focusable (tabindex=0, a button, or a link with href); assert every classified selector is seen somewhere and every control selector matches at least one element (non-vacuous both ways). Separately assert the only emitted tabindex values are 0 and -1, with -1 confined to roving tablist buttons.", "status": "Verified"}, "TC-118": {"tier": "tc", "title": "verifies SR-052;LLR-113", "body": "Every painted vocabulary member is explained in words in its own document; the tier legend is a TIER_FILL bijection (dict-derived, so a dropped member fails); the emitted JS tierColor/statusColor maps byte-match the Python palettes in every render; the CSS status tokens match STATUS_FILL and stay theme-invariant. Verified to fail against the stale hardcoded TC swatch, a legend entry going missing (the legend-less flat seam graph was caught live on this test's first run), the stale JS map (caught live on the committed artifact before its fix), a drifted --done token, and an emitter dropping a tier member.", "meta": "Method: Over the shipped dashboard plus seven fixture renders: resolve the document's token definitions, collect every legend swatch carrying a non-empty word label (var() resolved), collect every vocabulary member painted in a PAINT surface of the script-stripped markup (style blocks, style attributes, fill/stroke attributes), and assert each painted member's hex appears as a worded swatch in the SAME document; assert every vocabulary is exercised somewhere in the sweep. Plus the tier-legend bijection: the icicle legend's swatch list equals TIER_FILL in declaration order.", "status": "Verified"}, "TC-119": {"tier": "tc", "title": "verifies SR-052;LLR-114", "body": "Vocabulary set closed at five; every member clears both floors; every CSS fill token classified and floor-checked. Verified to fail against a rogue sixth vocabulary (flat AND nested shapes), an under-floor member (2.54:1), and an unclassified fill token.", "meta": "Method: Reflect every UPPERCASE module-level constant RECURSIVELY (nested dicts/tuples/sets and bare strings) for any 3/4/6/8-digit hex member and assert the hex-bearing set is exactly the five declared vocabularies, every member canonical 6-digit lowercase, and every member clearing 4.5:1 against its label ink (white, or the declared queued dark-ink exception) and 3:1 for its computed _ring_ink. Separately derive every fill:var() token from the emitted CSS and assert each carries a declared role, with white-text-fill roles clearing 4.5:1 under white and container-fill roles keeping --text readable, in BOTH themes. The six sibling A4 tests keep owning their specific arithmetic and are cited as evidence beside the closure.", "status": "Verified"}, "TC-120": {"tier": "tc", "title": "verifies SR-054;LLR-115", "body": "Each task's entry point is present, labelled, and <= 1 switch from the landing view; the next-work surface is non-empty under a zero-active registry. Verified to fail against the next-work surface dropped and against its label emitted empty (guard-bite; source restored byte-identical).", "meta": "Method: Generate the dashboard from a zero-active/all-queued fixture — the condition under which a next-work surface can exist in the emitter and render nothing plus a committed module map, then resolve each of the three core reading tasks' entry points from the emitted document and assert each is LABELLED and reachable in <= 1 tab switch: the landing Definition-completeness/Execution cards (task 1, 0 switches), the landing Next-work card (task 2, 0 switches), and the How-SW nav tab (task 3, 1 switch). Assert the next-work surface renders NAMED content (not an empty region) on the zero-active artifact; its non-emptiness across the waiting-with-predecessor and drained fixtures is owned by the next-work tests named in this row's Evidence.", "status": "Verified"}, "TC-121": {"tier": "tc", "title": "verifies SR-054;LLR-116", "body": "Every emitted svg scales to fit its container; zero svgs keep the pre-fix fixed-width shape; the shrink floor is pinned to the one declared constant rather than re-hardcoded in the test.", "meta": "Method: Generate the dashboard and derive EVERY emitted <svg> from the document (not a hand list, so a fourth emitter cannot skip the rule); assert each carries the responsive style and none keeps a bare fixed width; assert the emitted min/max ratio equals the declared SHRINK_FLOOR constant.", "status": "Verified"}, "TC-122": {"tier": "tc", "title": "verifies SR-054;LLR-117", "body": "One theme mechanism at :root; zero mixed-family pairs across 900+ classified node pairs and 12 CSS text fills; both families actually occur among the swept rect fills, so the sweep is not vacuous. Guard proven to bite on four independent mutations, each caught by its own assertion: dropping --text from the dark block (half-flip), a phase block's ink switched to var(--text) over its fixed fill, #ice .cell text switched to var(--text) over its invariant host, and a second prefers-color-scheme block scoped to .detail. Source restored byte-identical after each.", "meta": "Method: Sweep EVERY emitter document (the shipped artifact plus a fixture per emitter, the A2-review rule that a walk judges only what its fixture renders) and, per document: derive the theme-varying/-invariant token families from the emitted CSS; assert exactly one prefers-color-scheme block and one color-scheme declaration, both at :root; assert body's own background and ink are theme-varying; assert no CSS rule pairs a background and an ink from two families; assert no emitted SVG node pairs an inline rect fill with an inline text fill from two families. Then, accumulated ACROSS the sweep (because one document cannot distinguish -paints on the page background- from -this emitter does not render those nodes-), assert every CSS-declared SVG text fill matches the family its host nodes actually paint, or is theme-varying when it has no host anywhere.", "status": "Verified"}, "TC-123": {"tier": "tc", "title": "verifies SR-049;LLR-118", "body": "Every assertion holds, each with its negative half. Three defects were caught by these guards during the build and fixed rather than accommodated: a missing UTF-8 console guard, a changed-percent diluted by whitespace tokens, and bootstrap leaving __pycache__ in a fresh scaffold once a generator imported its siblings.", "meta": "Method: Drive gen_open_items over temp repos: assert a pending registry row renders as a brief and a RULED row does not; that Draft AND Modified spine rows both surface (ratification owed vs re-attest owed) while a Verified row does not; that a section with no changed cells says CHECK THE BASELINE and never nothing-changed; that --check bites on drift, MASKS the machine-local region (and still bites outside it), and re-reads the baseline stamp the file declares; that the whole thing is vacuous with neither registry nor view; that registry prose is HTML-escaped; that the word diff marks only what moved and the percentage counts words not whitespace; and that the theme tokens equal the dashboard's emitted values (a drift guard, not an extraction).", "status": "Verified"}, "TC-124": {"tier": "tc", "title": "verifies SR-054;LLR-119", "body": "Zero label lines outside their own block across every drill block of the emitted document; the sentence-length need present among them. Guard proven to bite on the original defect: reverted to the pre-fix emitter it fails naming SN-001's ink at x=-241..449 in a block spanning x=18..190, and the fit-path and helper guards fail with it, while the two-line-grid guard correctly passes both before and after (it guards over-application, not the defect). Source restored byte-identical. Second half: the 109-character clause renders whole; past the bound the disclosure is present, operable and lossless. Both proven to bite on the pre-fix emitter, which renders the critic's exact string 'tiering expo…' and has no _NEXT_WORK_TITLE bound at all. Source restored byte-identical.", "meta": "Method: Generate the dashboard over a tiered fixture carrying one sentence-length stakeholder need (the shape that overflowed), then sweep EVERY drill block in the emitted document - not a per-view list, because the defect lives in the one shared label emitter that feeds four views. For each block, take its rect and each label line's own x/dy from the markup, measure the line's ink with the emitter's declared per-character widths and the font sizes the emitted CSS declares (unescaping entities first, so an apostrophe is one glyph and not six), and assert the ink box lies inside the rect on both axes. Assert the sentence-length need is actually among the swept labels, so the sweep cannot pass vacuously; separately assert the fit path itself (a second line broken on a word, then an ellipsis, with the full string still reachable) and that a sub-label which already fits keeps the untouched two-line grid. Second half: render the next-work card from a fixture carrying the 109-character _NW_LONG clause and assert it appears WHOLE with no ellipsis in the list, the fixture asserted longer than the retired 60-character budget so the check cannot pass vacuously; then, from a fixture past the declared bound, assert a native details/summary with a visible cue, that the emitted head and remainder rejoin to exactly the clause and the cut fell on a word, and that the reveal is neither script-dependent nor hidden by the emitter's own CSS.", "status": "Verified"}, "TC-125": {"tier": "tc", "title": "verifies SR-054;LLR-120", "body": "Zero wires through a non-endpoint node box; the sweep non-vacuous (wires present, at least one detoured). Guard proven to bite: with the router's blocked-wire branch disabled so every wire keeps its direct cubic, it fails naming a knowledge-graph wire cutting the 'Low-Level Requirement' node at (330,18,96,46). Source restored byte-identical.", "meta": "Method: Sweep the union of emitter documents (the shipped PROJECT_STATE.html plus a fixture per emitter - the A2-review rule that a walk judges only what its fixture renders) and, per emitted <svg>: parse every node's id and rect and every wire's path data, sample each path into the polyline the router's own hit-test uses (so the test and the emitter describe one curve), drop the rects whose own port circle holds an endpoint, and assert the polyline crosses none of the rest. Assert the sweep found wires at all AND that at least one of them is a DETOUR, so a broken router cannot pass a sweep in which nothing needed re-routing.", "status": "Verified"}, "TC-126": {"tier": "tc", "title": "verifies SR-126;LLR-133", "body": "Satisfies SR-126 AcceptanceCriteria", "meta": "Method: Run the spine stand-alone suite; a WI id or process-doc citation in a normative cell of any spine registry is a finding, and a script name, artifact path, rubric or sibling id is not.", "status": "Verified"}, "TC-127": {"tier": "tc", "title": "verifies SR-127;LLR-134", "body": "Satisfies SR-127 AcceptanceCriteria", "meta": "Method: Run the requirement-form suite; each of the six rules fires on its own defect shape, and the negative half (Draft, zero-`shall`, `must`, a multi-clause AcceptanceCriteria, a passive with a named actor) does not.", "status": "Verified"}, "TC-128": {"tier": "tc", "title": "verifies SR-128;LLR-135", "body": "Satisfies SR-128 AcceptanceCriteria", "meta": "Method: Run the paraphrase-advisory suite; an echoing child warns while a real decomposition naming module and mechanism does not, and the exit code is unchanged either way.", "status": "Verified"}, "TC-129": {"tier": "tc", "title": "verifies SR-129;LLR-136", "body": "Satisfies SR-129 AcceptanceCriteria", "meta": "Method: Run the converter suite: the live registry round-trips in whichever home is authoritative; an unknown status is refused by name; a corrupted rebuilt spec reds the cell comparison after a clean-first control; folder->CSV->folder is parse-equal including a hand-filed spec.", "status": "Verified"}, "TC-130": {"tier": "tc", "title": "verifies SR-130;LLR-137", "body": "Satisfies SR-130 AcceptanceCriteria", "meta": "Method: Run the trunk-step suite: committed fragments compile in git order with links rebased and fragments deleted; an uncommitted, heading-less or reserved-heading fragment blocks the whole batch; a fragment-free run is a clean idempotent no-op.", "status": "Verified"}, "TC-131": {"tier": "tc", "title": "verifies SR-131;LLR-138", "body": "Satisfies SR-131 AcceptanceCriteria", "meta": "Method: Run the pause suites: the tracked home pauses via pause_reason with the unchanged return contract; a stray legacy file is inert; malformation pauses fail-closed with the pinned loud placeholder.", "status": "Verified"}, "TC-132": {"tier": "tc", "title": "verifies SR-132;LLR-140", "body": "Satisfies SR-132 AcceptanceCriteria", "meta": "Method: Run the integrator suite: each claim refusal fires by name and the green claim moves the spec and cuts the branch; finished-branch detection keys on the tree; the verdict gate refuses absent, CHANGES-REQUESTED and stale-APPROVE verdicts and passes a fresh APPROVE; a missing or empty bar declaration refuses; the window audit flags a non-merge product commit and passes a bookkeeping-only window; one end-to-end claim->work->close->integrate run fast-forwards the trunk to a --no-ff merge commit.", "status": "Verified"}, "TC-133": {"tier": "tc", "title": "verifies SR-061;SR-062;SR-065;SR-095;SR-096;SR-097;SR-098;SR-099;SR-100;SR-101;SR-117;SR-118;SR-119;SR-120;SR-121", "body": "All frozen links resolve and are acyclic; no legacy row retains an LLR; this TC cites every Phase-5 legacy row.", "meta": "Method: Inspect the fifteen Phase-5 legacy SR rows, their SupersededBy links to SR-132, and the post-deletion registries.", "status": "Verified"}, "TC-134": {"tier": "tc", "title": "verifies SR-133;LLR-141", "body": "Satisfies SR-133 AcceptanceCriteria", "meta": "Method: Run the check-harness lane suite: a claimed work branch skips the declared freshness steps with the §5.2 notice and untouched exit code while non-freshness steps still run; the closing commit and its successors keep the skip (history-derived signal); the trunk lane never skips.", "status": "Verified"}, "TC-135": {"tier": "tc", "title": "verifies SR-134;LLR-142", "body": "Satisfies SR-134 AcceptanceCriteria", "meta": "Method: Run the trunk-step regen suite: --regen skips absent artifact families with a notice and stops loudly at the first failing generator, regenerating in dependency order.", "status": "Verified"}, "TC-136": {"tier": "tc", "title": "verifies SR-135;LLR-139", "body": "Satisfies SR-135 AcceptanceCriteria", "meta": "Method: Run the pending-surface pause suite: the block renders since/reason verbatim (no clock), omits the stamp when since is empty, matches the reader's fail-closed placeholder on malformation, clears on deletion, and is deterministic.", "status": "Verified"}, "TC-137": {"tier": "tc", "title": "verifies SR-026;LLR-143", "body": "Satisfies SR-026 AcceptanceCriteria", "meta": "Method: Run the drive suite: an unwired agent command refuses before any claim while an empty queue still drains to exit 0; a refusing claim rung, a stranded claim, a dirty trunk and a red composed-tree bar each stop the run by name; the tracked pause appearing mid-run stops the next cycle at exit 8; NEEDS-HUMAN propagates at exit 7 with the claim parked; a DONE-reporting worker that finishes nothing trips the stall guard; and two end-to-end runs against the real bar prove the green path (claim->build->merge->drained banner) and the red path (candidate parked, claim intact). The plain agent_loop.py launch enters the drive mode as a subprocess.", "status": "Verified"}, "TC-138": {"tier": "tc", "title": "verifies SR-132;LLR-144", "body": "Satisfies SR-132 AcceptanceCriteria", "meta": "Method: Run the handback suite: a partial close moves each claimed spec to the terminal partial/ and writes its immutable per-close report under docs/handbacks/, leaves the branch finished, is CLEAN under the real trajectory check (R-A exempts partial — the spec's definition is deliberately byte-identical), refuses a second close without residue, and is LOUD when a terminal spec has no report; an already-declared blockref and an existing Deliverable survive; a branch trunk holds no claim for is refused. The quarantine arm reverts the product paths and keeps the failing diff as a bar-inert .patch, reverts a RENAME correctly (the --name-status -z stream read as records, not pairs - mutation-proven), leaves the handback bookkeeping alone, refuses when the red is not the lane's own code, and restores rather than reports when a revert step fails.", "status": "Modified"}, "TC-139": {"tier": "tc", "title": "verifies SR-132;LLR-145", "body": "Satisfies SR-132 AcceptanceCriteria", "meta": "Method: Run the spec_move suite: an archival move redirects inbound links from every depth (text untouched, fragments carried, external URLs and bare anchors left alone), rebases the moved spec's own links one directory deeper, preserves CRLF on both sides, and stages a git mv when the tree is a repo; the REAL check_docs passes over the archived fixture while the MUTATION TWIN - the same move without the rebase - fails it, so the guard reproduces the defect it fixes; a move with rewritten text (the handback shape) still runs the whole ritual; a missing source and an existing destination refuse; the CLI archives to the dated destination and refuses nonzero. The wired call sites are driven in their own suites: integrate.claim runs the ritual inside the one claim commit and a crashed relinked claim still re-cuts while a non-relink .md edit convicts (tests/test_integrate.py); the handback return runs it in reverse (tests/test_handback.py).", "status": "Verified"}, "TC-140": {"tier": "tc", "title": "verifies SR-136;LLR-146", "body": "Satisfies SR-136 AcceptanceCriteria", "meta": "Method: Run the figure-provenance suite: the three 2026-08-01 false figures (the stale mutation ledger, the unreproducible link count, the digitless two-false-positives) each flag under a bare fig: marker, warn-first then gating under --strict; a cmd= plus rev= marker and a non-empty derived= marker pass; a half-carrying or empty-valued marker names its missing half; unmarked figure prose stays out of scope with the claim stated; fig-ok lines and GENERATED blocks are exempt; config:-shaped words never match; docs/stack.ini is scanned beside the markdown surfaces; a fresh bootstrap scaffold passes the docstring opt-in end-to-end; placeholder-grammar examples and a docs/reviews/ record quoting defective markers declare nothing; a wordless rev= counts as missing; two half-carrying markers on one line are two findings; a quoted rev= is accepted; a defective marker whose cmd= embeds shell metacharacters still flags its missing rev=; a declaration whose command legitimately redirects is counted and passes; a mixed marker - one real value beside a wholly-placeholder one - is judged as a real marker whose placeholder value counts as missing, flagging the missing half both ways (a real cmd= with a placeholder rev=, a placeholder cmd= with a real rev=).", "status": "Verified"}, "TC-141": {"tier": "tc", "title": "verifies SR-049;LLR-147", "body": "Satisfies SR-049 AcceptanceCriteria", "meta": "Method: Fixture-drive the SN-coverage rung: an uncovered ratified SN caps raw at G0 (the runnable value floors to G1) with uncovered=1 on the basis line and drafts=0; citing the need from an SR's SN-Refs restores the prior level (uncovered=0, G3); a Draft SN keeps riding the draft rung with uncovered=0 (the double-counting seam - one fact, one rung); -000 rows on both sides of the join are ignored, so an example SR row cannot fake coverage of a real need; the ex-draft counterfactual rebuilds the cited set over the non-draft subset, so a need answered only by a Draft SR reads G0 there too; and the sn_cited_ids parse is pinned equal between trace.py and derive_gate.py across the separator/empty/absent-cell battery (tests/test_rule_sync.py).", "status": "Verified"}, "TC-142": {"tier": "tc", "title": "verifies SR-049;LLR-148", "body": "Satisfies SR-049 AcceptanceCriteria", "meta": "Method: Fixture-drive --next-phase: on a spine whose non-draft max phase is 3 with a Draft row at 4 it prints 4 (a Draft phase is not yet scope) and leaves docs/gate byte-identical (output mode only); on an unphased spine it prints 2 (the implicit foundation is 1).", "status": "Verified"}, "TC-143": {"tier": "tc", "title": "verifies SR-093;LLR-149", "body": "Satisfies SR-093 AcceptanceCriteria", "meta": "Method: Run the dispatch admission suite: an exclusive row + a busy lane answers wait (never a parallel claim slipped past the barrier) while the same frontier without one keeps filling lanes; lanes back -> every spine row admits as ONE batch ahead of ordinary work; the §A8 table verbatim per kind x level (attended surfaces attestation/gate rows, single-ratify keeps non-dependent work and admits the queued ratification batch only at the close, autonomous dispatches them exclusive); the lanes ladder resolves CLI > AGENT_LANES > stack.ini > 1 with absent/malformed/sub-1 falling to serial; gap_census names unverified SRs, orphan rows and draft SNs mechanically and answers [] on a registry-less repo; kind_of agrees with classify at every quarantine.", "status": "Verified"}, "TC-144": {"tier": "tc", "title": "verifies SR-132;LLR-150", "body": "Satisfies SR-132 AcceptanceCriteria", "meta": "Method: Run the dispatch loop suite on real git repos with the real bar: a spine batch claims as one commit and its worker receives both ids together, ordinary work admitted only after the window closes; a NEEDS-HUMAN worker hands back, the lane's refresh runs as its own subprocess and the branch merges; a red refresh quarantines a merges-nothing branch once and stops the run for a done-asserting one; an attended gate row drains and exits 0 with the ratifications banner; the empty-frontier ladder hands the gap census to the intake mint (rows minted in one bookkeeping commit, driven by the same run, deduped on the next idle pass) and counts rung-2 cards off the shared pending read; pause/dirty-trunk/stall/crash-resume keep their serial-loop contracts at lanes=1.", "status": "Verified"}, "TC-145": {"tier": "tc", "title": "verifies SR-132;LLR-151", "body": "Satisfies SR-132 AcceptanceCriteria", "meta": "Method: Run the integrator claim suite: a spine claim succeeds on an idle station (the deleted safety-class arm, red-then-green); a hand claim while another holder has the dispatch lock refuses naming the lock and leaves the queue untouched, while dispatch_lock_held=True proceeds; a spine batch claims as ONE bookkeeping commit whose subject joins the ids and whose specs all land in active/<branch>/; every pre-existing single-WI claim contract (abandoned-claim re-cut, relink oracle, minted-id rung, RULING-6 audit) holds unchanged.", "status": "Verified"}, "TC-146": {"tier": "tc", "title": "verifies SR-093;LLR-152", "body": "Satisfies SR-093 AcceptanceCriteria", "meta": "Method: Run the schedule + integrate suites' adjudication cases: the kind classifies exclusive at rank 1 (the reserved slot, pinned by name); an adjudication-only lane's refresh runs NO bar yet still commits a verified Bar-Green attestation whose summary says no-bar, while a mixed batch bars as usual (fail toward the bar); bar = G2 reaches check.py as --gate G2 (asserted off the recording stub's own argv), an undeclared bar passes no --gate, and a malformed value refuses the refresh naming it.", "status": "Verified"}, "TC-147": {"tier": "tc", "title": "verifies SR-132;LLR-153;IF-091", "body": "Satisfies SR-132 AcceptanceCriteria", "meta": "Method: Run the intake suite against real git repos, red-then-green per trigger (trigger (b) keys on the close's immutable REPORT PATH, so a re-sweep dedupes exactly and a genuinely second close is a second row): a ratified SR amendment mints ONE adjudication row (id max+1, blockref empty, the before/after listing in ## Context) and an LLR SR-Refs re-point mints while a Module-only move stays silent (the ruled routing); a merged handback mints the disposition row (NEEDS-HUMAN reason routes strong; a handed-back adjudication row mints NOTHING and its own handback attempt is refused structurally); a merged adjudication row's ## Dispositions drafts mint at its merge with planmode=dual passing through kind-derived, and a malformed block, an unknown key, a second adjudication kind or a bad bar value refuse with nothing minted; the census mints gap rows once and dedupes on re-run; every re-run is idempotent by exact-title dedup; the context block renders every join in failure-cost order and answers the empty string on a bare repo; both gate-policy arms enact (attended recommends and leaves the registries byte-identical; single-ratify and autonomous flip only the named Status cells, cell-exact elsewhere, idempotent).", "status": "Modified"}, "TC-148": {"tier": "tc", "title": "verifies SR-132;LLR-154;IF-090", "body": "Satisfies SR-132 AcceptanceCriteria", "meta": "Method: Run the integrator + dispatcher suites' intake-arm cases: a merged branch that amended a ratified SR cell yields the adjudication row as its own mint: commit immediately after the merge commit on trunk (in-slot, serial); the dispatcher's empty-frontier rung 1 mints gap rows and KEEPS DRIVING them in the same run, then exits honestly when every gap already carries a row; a census-mint refusal stops the run loudly; the handback loop tests drive the disposition row the same run mints.", "status": "Verified"}, "TC-149": {"tier": "tc", "title": "verifies SR-034", "body": "Satisfies the shipped-tier clause of SR-034 AcceptanceCriteria", "meta": "Method: Run the shipped-tier suite; it derives the adopter-facing check set from check.py's own layer=process step tags, walks their transitive sibling imports, and asserts every non-stdlib module in that closure is a Kind=python ledger row that is Tier=shipped with a non-empty Ruled cell. Mutation proofs drive the checker over fixture trees carrying a coordinator-tier, an unruled shipped, and an undeclared import and assert each is caught.", "status": "Verified"}, "TC-150": {"tier": "tc", "title": "verifies SR-137;LLR-155", "body": "Satisfies SR-137 AcceptanceCriteria", "meta": "Method: Run the process-config suite: it sources the SHIPPED hook's own sh functions and drives them against `tomllib` over a table of adversarial file shapes (trailing comments, dotted keys, inline tables, uppercase TRUE, BOM, CRLF, wrong section), asserts the two agree on every shape and that an unparseable file reads ON in both, and drives the mixed-config refusal and the wrong-typed-dial refusal.", "status": "Draft"}, "TC-151": {"tier": "tc", "title": "verifies SR-139;LLR-155;LLR-157", "body": "Satisfies SR-139 AcceptanceCriteria", "meta": "Method: Run the ratification-level suite: the full level x stage matrix against the ladder the shipped template documents, every malformed input (negative, out-of-range, string, float, bool, absent, unparseable), the legacy-word translation, and the spine-stage corners (draft need, empty spine, uncited need, Modified SR, missing child, LLR-exempt SR).", "status": "Draft"}, "TC-152": {"tier": "tc", "title": "verifies SR-138;LLR-156", "body": "Satisfies SR-138 AcceptanceCriteria", "meta": "Method: Run the migration cases in the process-config suite: a full conversion deletes every legacy file and lands all three ratification dials; a second pass is a no-op; a hand-trimmed process.toml leaves the legacy file in place with its value intact; the F5 translation tables are pinned equal and the retired enum key is absent from the shipped template.", "status": "Draft"}, "TC-153": {"tier": "tc", "title": "verifies SR-140;LLR-158", "body": "Satisfies SR-140 AcceptanceCriteria", "meta": "Method: Run the attestation-digest suite: it DRIVES the premise rather than asserting it - the amendment seam is shown blind to a sanctioned amend+flip over a real two-commit git repo, which is why an anchor recorded at acceptance time is owed at all - then pins what the digest is taken over (a traced cell and the Status marker must not move it; a ratified cell must), that a need's digest is its raw table line and survives re-indentation, and that current_digests covers every real spine row and every real need while excluding -000 rows and ids that appear only in prose.", "status": "Draft"}, "TC-154": {"tier": "tc", "title": "verifies SR-141;SR-142;LLR-159", "body": "Satisfies SR-141 and SR-142 AcceptanceCriteria", "meta": "Method: Run the loop-order suite: an adjudication row admits ahead of a ready spine batch while the ruled rank table is unchanged; the partition is stable and cannot move work past a human-held stop; a red TC is named only under a `done` citer, with the three exempt statuses and the mixed-target case driven; the census grammar round-trips and matches nothing else.", "status": "Draft"}, "TC-155": {"tier": "tc", "title": "verifies SR-143;LLR-160", "body": "Satisfies SR-143 AcceptanceCriteria", "meta": "Method: Run the queue-conflict cases: each of the three signals fires with both ids in deterministic order, a closed row never conflicts, unrelated open rows and a shared stopword are silent, and the findings are wired on the warn-only line rather than into the exit code.", "status": "Draft"}, "TC-156": {"tier": "tc", "title": "verifies SR-144;SR-145;LLR-161", "body": "Satisfies SR-144 and SR-145 AcceptanceCriteria", "meta": "Method: Run the handback suite over real git worktrees: a partial close is clean under the REAL trajectory check (not a stub), a terminal spec with no report is loud, a second close is refused and leaves no residue, and the disposition is keyed on the report path so a re-sweep mints nothing.", "status": "Draft"}, "TC-157": {"tier": "tc", "title": "verifies SR-146;LLR-162;LLR-163", "body": "Satisfies SR-146 AcceptanceCriteria", "meta": "Method: Run the prompts and routing suites: strict slot filling and its refusals, the preflight on a missing template, the catalogue's freshness gate, the digest's line-ending normalization, the argv-array form with its fall-through and refusal cases, and the ADJUDICATE phase's tier, cross-family rule and escalation deafness.", "status": "Draft"}, "TC-158": {"tier": "tc", "title": "verifies SR-132;IF-101", "body": "A live id above its mark, a missing space, a malformed line, an absent file, a lowered mark and a hand-raised mark each fail loud; headroom left by a deleted row stays legal; the mint returns the next unused id after a deletion and refuses without a mark.", "meta": "Method: Run the id-watermark suite. It drives trace.py's CLI so the rules are asserted on the EXIT CODE, not just as a function call - the wiring into --strict-integrity is the guarantee, and a suite that only calls watermark_findings() survived deleting it. Covers the mint seam IF-101 declares: next_wi_id counts from the mark, so a deleted id is not re-issued, and the reader's refusal on an absent mark is NOT caught.", "status": "Draft"}, "TC-159": {"tier": "tc", "title": "verifies SR-147;LLR-165", "body": "Satisfies SR-147 AcceptanceCriteria", "meta": "Method: Run the carrier-converter suite: it converts the live spine, re-parses the emitted TOML with tomllib and asserts the round-trip is cell-for-cell identical to the source for every row of every tier, then DRIVES the loss detector against corruption classes (a dropped row, a dropped field, a truncated value, a re-typed value, a mangled ref list) and asserts each is REFUSED with a finding naming the row and field, so the clean result is evidence rather than a check that cannot fail.", "status": "Draft"}, "TC-160": {"tier": "tc", "title": "verifies SR-147;LLR-166", "body": "Satisfies SR-147 AcceptanceCriteria", "meta": "Method: Drive the carrier reader over a REAL repo whose spine is cut over from CSV to TOML in one commit, and assert the four properties that fail open if wrong: the pre-migration revision still reads through the carrier it used then; the post-migration revision reads through the new one presenting the same column names; a lossless cutover is SILENT to the amendment guard while text smuggled into that same commit is NAMED with its row and cell; and a carrier that does not parse - including the duplicate id the carrier turns into a decode error - is reported absent rather than empty. Then pin the vocabulary against drift: the reader is the exact inverse of the writer's KEY, and every column of every LIVE spine header is driven through the pair so the agreement cannot be vacuous.", "status": "Draft"}}, archDesc = {"TC-010": [], "LLR-010": ["TC-010"], "SR-010": ["LLR-010", "TC-010"], "TC-011": [], "LLR-011": ["TC-011"], "SR-011": ["LLR-011", "TC-011"], "TC-032": [], "LLR-032": ["TC-032"], "SR-032": ["LLR-032", "TC-032"], "TC-036": [], "SR-036": ["TC-036"], "TC-047": [], "LLR-047": ["TC-047"], "SR-046": ["LLR-047", "TC-047"], "LLR-121": [], "SR-111": ["LLR-121"], "LLR-122": [], "SR-113": ["LLR-122"], "SN-001": ["SR-010", "LLR-010", "TC-010", "SR-011", "LLR-011", "TC-011", "SR-032", "LLR-032", "TC-032", "SR-036", "TC-036", "SR-046", "LLR-047", "TC-047", "SR-111", "LLR-121", "SR-113", "LLR-122"], "TC-001": [], "LLR-001": ["TC-001"], "SR-001": ["LLR-001", "TC-001"], "TC-002": [], "LLR-002": ["TC-002"], "SR-002": ["LLR-002", "TC-002"], "TC-004": [], "LLR-004": ["TC-004"], "SR-004": ["LLR-004", "TC-004"], "TC-005": [], "LLR-005": ["TC-005"], "SR-005": ["LLR-005", "TC-005"], "TC-015": [], "LLR-015": ["TC-015"], "SR-015": ["LLR-015", "TC-015"], "TC-024": [], "LLR-024": ["TC-024"], "SR-024": ["LLR-024", "TC-024"], "TC-099": [], "SR-037": ["TC-099"], "TC-037": [], "LLR-034": ["TC-037"], "SR-067": ["LLR-034", "TC-037"], "TC-077": [], "LLR-077": ["TC-077"], "SR-068": ["LLR-077", "TC-077"], "TC-075": [], "LLR-075": ["TC-075"], "SR-069": ["LLR-075", "TC-075"], "TC-100": [], "LLR-097": ["TC-100"], "SR-109": ["LLR-097", "TC-100"], "TC-126": [], "LLR-133": ["TC-126"], "SR-126": ["LLR-133", "TC-126"], "TC-127": [], "LLR-134": ["TC-127"], "SR-127": ["LLR-134", "TC-127"], "TC-128": [], "LLR-135": ["TC-128"], "SR-128": ["LLR-135", "TC-128"], "TC-129": [], "LLR-136": ["TC-129"], "SR-129": ["LLR-136", "TC-129"], "TC-159": [], "LLR-165":