/h3><p class="baseline">baseline a5052a913 (2026-07-25) — from --since</p><div class="row"><div class="row-head"><span class="rid">SR SR-031</span><span class="pill">changed</span></div><div class="cellname">Requirement <span class="pill">80% of the words changed</span></div><div class="diff"><span class="eq">The </span><del>gate-policy, push-policy, and privacy-check</del><ins>policy</ins><span class="eq"> readers shall share one </span><del>declared-value </del><span class="eq">parse so the hooks, </span><del>agent_loop,</del><ins>agent_loop</ins><span class="eq"> and check_privacy agree on </span><ins>every declared value. Since SN-028 that parse is docs/process.toml, read by two grammars — tomllib and </ins><span class="eq">the </span><del>value.</del><ins>hooks&#x27; pure sh — whose agreement over the file&#x27;s checked line shape is itself driven; the legacy one-word files stay readable through the migration window, and a dial declared in both homes is REFUSED rather than resolved by precedence.</ins></div><div class="cellname">AcceptanceCriteria <span class="pill">92% of the words changed</span></div><div class="diff"><del>The gate-policy and push-policy readers return the first declared line; every</del><ins>Every</ins><span class="eq"> enforcer reads the same </span><del>value.</del><ins>value for the same dial; the hooks&#x27; sh and tomllib return the same answer over the adversarial file-shape table (including a trailing-comment decoy, which once made the privacy gate fail OPEN); a legacy file present alongside its key is a refusal naming both.</ins></div><div class="ctx"><div class="ctxhead">the rest of this SR — unchanged since the baseline</div><div class="field"><span class="k">SR-ID</span><span class="v">SR-031</span></div><div class="field"><span class="k">Title</span><span class="v">Declared-policy readers agree</span></div><div class="field"><span class="k">SN-Refs</span><span class="v">SN-004;SN-005</span></div><div class="field"><span class="k">Rationale</span><span class="v">Realizes SN-004 (policies drive the gate) and SN-005 (one source, every enforcer reads it the same way).</span></div><div class="field"><span class="k">Priority</span><span class="v">M</span></div><div class="field"><span class="k">Verification</span><span class="v">Test</span></div><div class="field"><span class="k">Status</span><span class="v">Modified</span></div><div class="field"><span class="k">Phase</span><span class="v">1</span></div><div class="field"><span class="k">Area</span><span class="v">Declared-policy readers</span></div></div></div><div class="row"><div class="row-head"><span class="rid">TC TC-031</span><span class="pill">changed</span></div><div class="cellname">Method <span class="pill">88% of the words changed</span></div><div class="diff"><span class="eq">Run the </span><del>gate-policy</del><ins>process-config</ins><span class="eq"> and </span><del>push-policy</del><ins>policy</ins><span class="eq"> </span><del>suites;</del><ins>suites:</ins><span class="eq"> </span><del>each</del><ins>every</ins><span class="eq"> </span><del>reader</del><ins>enforcer</ins><span class="eq"> </span><del>returns</del><ins>reads one value per dial from docs/process.toml,</ins><span class="eq"> the </span><del>first</del><ins>hooks&#x27;</ins><span class="eq"> </span><del>declared</del><ins>sh</ins><span class="eq"> </span><del>line.</del><ins>and tomllib agree over the adversarial shape table, and a mixed config is refused.</ins></div><div class="ctx"><div class="ctxhead">the rest of this TC — unchanged since the baseline</div><div class="field"><span class="k">TC-ID</span><span class="v">TC-031</span></div><div class="field"><span class="k">Verifies</span><span class="v">SR-031;LLR-031</span></div><div class="field"><span class="k">Level</span><span class="v">Integration</span></div><div class="field"><span class="k">Tier</span><span class="v">Full</span></div><div class="field"><span class="k">Expected</span><span class="v">Satisfies SR-031 AcceptanceCriteria</span></div><div class="field"><span class="k">Automated</span><span class="v">Yes</span></div><div class="field"><span class="k">Evidence</span><span class="v">tests/test_gate_policy.py;tests/test_push_policy.py</span></div><div class="field"><span class="k">Status</span><span class="v">Modified</span></div><div class="field"><span class="k">Phase</span><span class="v">1</span></div></div></div></article><article class="card" id="SR-034-attest"><h3><span class="rid">SR-034</span><span>Kit scripts run on stdlib plus ledger-declared dependencies</span><span class="pill">re-attest owed</span></h3><p class="baseline">baseline a5052a913 (2026-07-25) — from --since</p><div class="row"><div class="row-head"><span class="rid">SR SR-034</span><span class="pill">changed</span></div><div class="cellname">Title <span class="pill">100% of the words changed</span></div><div class="diff"><del>Scripts</del><ins>Kit</ins><span class="eq"> </span><del>are</del><ins>scripts</ins><span class="eq"> </span><del>stdlib-only</del><ins>run on stdlib plus ledger-declared dependencies</ins></div><div class="cellname">Requirement <span class="pill">58% of the words changed</span></div><div class="diff"><span class="eq">Every kit script shall run on a clean Python 3.11+ </span><del>with</del><ins>using</ins><span class="eq"> </span><del>no</del><ins>the</ins><span class="eq"> </span><del>pip installs (standard</del><ins>standard</ins><span class="eq"> library </span><del>only).</del><ins>plus only those non-stdlib dependencies declared as a reviewed row in docs/dependencies.md.</ins></div><div class="cellname">Rationale <span class="pill">81% of the words changed</span></div><div class="diff"><span class="eq">Realizes SN-011 — the kit </span><del>imposes</del><ins>must impose</ins><span class="eq"> no</span><ins> *unargued*</ins><span class="eq"> dependency stack on a downstream repo to run its </span><del>checks.</del><ins>checks, but a blanket ban is itself a design constraint that can force a worse hand-rolled alternative than a well-chosen tool, so the bar is a reviewed argument per dependency (owner RULING-3, 2026-07-28), not abstinence. Leaving the row at &quot;stdlib-only&quot; was rejected: it had already drifted from the standing ruling, leaving the registry and the ledger giving two answers to one question.</ins></div><div class="cellname">AcceptanceCriteria <span class="pill">88% of the words changed</span></div><div class="diff"><del>No kit script imports a third-party package; an</del><ins>An</ins><span class="eq"> AST scan </span><del>asserts</del><ins>of scripts/*.py resolves</ins><span class="eq"> every top-level import </span><del>in scripts/*.py resolves </del><span class="eq">to </span><del>stdlib</del><ins>stdlib, a local sibling,</ins><span class="eq"> or a </span><del>local</del><ins>Kind=python</ins><span class="eq"> </span><del>sibling.</del><ins>row in docs/dependencies.md; an undeclared non-stdlib import fails the suite; every declared row names what it replaces, why hand-rolling is worse, and the ruling that admitted it; a shipped-tier row (one an adopter is forced to install) exists only with an owner ruling recorded in the ledger, stdlib remaining preferred there.</ins></div><div class="ctx"><div class="ctxhead">the rest of this SR — unchanged since the baseline</div><div class="field"><span class="k">SR-ID</span><span class="v">SR-034</span></div><div class="field"><span class="k">SN-Refs</span><span class="v">SN-011</span></div><div class="field"><span class="k">Priority</span><span class="v">M</span></div><div class="field"><span class="k">Verification</span><span class="v">Analysis</span></div><div class="field"><span class="k">Status</span><span class="v">Modified</span></div><div class="field"><span class="k">Phase</span><span class="v">1</span></div><div class="field"><span class="k">Area</span><span class="v">Portability</span></div></div></div><div class="row"><div class="row-head"><span class="rid">TC TC-034</span><span class="pill">changed</span></div><div class="cellname">Method <span class="pill">55% of the words changed</span></div><div class="diff"><span class="eq">Run the </span><del>stdlib-only</del><ins>dependency-ledger</ins><span class="eq"> suite; an AST scan asserts every kit script&#x27;s top-level imports resolve to </span><del>stdlib or</del><ins>stdlib,</ins><span class="eq"> a local sibling, </span><ins>or a Kind=python row in docs/dependencies.md, </ins><span class="eq">and the </span><del>detector</del><ins>scanner</ins><span class="eq"> </span><del>flags</del><ins>is driven over</ins><span class="eq"> a </span><del>synthetic</del><ins>fixture</ins><span class="eq"> </span><del>third-party</del><ins>tree</ins><span class="eq"> </span><del>import.</del><ins>with a genuinely undeclared import to prove it catches one.</ins></div><div class="cellname">Evidence <span class="pill">100% of the words changed</span></div><div class="diff"><del>tests/test_stdlib_only.py</del><ins>tests/test_dependency_ledger.py</ins></div><div class="ctx"><div class="ctxhead">the rest of this TC — unchanged since the baseline</div><div class="field"><span class="k">TC-ID</span><span class="v">TC-034</span></div><div class="field"><span class="k">Verifies</span><span class="v">SR-034</span></div><div class="field"><span class="k">Level</span><span class="v">Analysis</span></div><div class="field"><span class="k">Tier</span><span class="v">Full</span></div><div class="field"><span class="k">Expected</span><span class="v">Satisfies SR-034 AcceptanceCriteria</span></div><div class="field"><span class="k">Automated</span><span class="v">Yes</span></div><div class="field"><span class="k">Status</span><span class="v">Modified</span></div><div class="field"><span class="k">Phase</span><span class="v">1</span></div></div></div><div class="row"><div class="row-head"><span class="rid">TC TC-149</span><span class="pill">ADDED since baseline</span></div><div class="cellname">TC-ID</div><div class="diff">TC-149</div><div class="cellname">Verifies</div><div class="diff">SR-034</div><div class="cellname">Level</div><div class="diff">Analysis</div><div class="cellname">Method</div><div class="diff">Run the shipped-tier suite; it derives the adopter-facing check set from check.py&#x27;s own layer=process step tags, walks their transitive sibling imports, and asserts every non-stdlib module in that closure is a Kind=python ledger row that is Tier=shipped with a non-empty Ruled cell. Mutation proofs drive the checker over fixture trees carrying a coordinator-tier, an unruled shipped, and an undeclared import and assert each is caught.</div><div class="cellname">Tier</div><div class="diff">Full</div><div class="cellname">Expected</div><div class="diff">Satisfies the shipped-tier clause of SR-034 AcceptanceCriteria</div><div class="cellname">Automated</div><div class="diff">Yes</div><div class="cellname">Evidence</div><div class="diff">tests/test_shipped_tier.py</div><div class="cellname">Status</div><div class="diff">Verified</div><div class="cellname">Phase</div><div class="diff">1</div></div></article><article class="card" id="SR-035-attest"><h3><span class="rid">SR-035</span><span>Stack-agnostic across OSes</span><span class="pill">re-attest owed</span></h3><p class="baseline">baseline a5052a913 (2026-07-25) — from --since</p><div class="row"><div class="row-head"><span class="rid">SR SR-035</span><span class="pill">changed</span></div><div class="cellname">Requirement <span class="pill">12% of the words changed</span></div><div class="diff"><span class="eq">The process and ID scheme shall be </span><del>stack-agnostic and the scripts shall run on Python 3.11+ across Linux, Windows and macOS.</del><ins>stack-agnostic.</ins></div><div class="cellname">Rationale <span class="pill">88% of the words changed</span></div><div class="diff"><span class="eq">Realizes SN-003 </span><del>and SN-011 </del><span class="eq">— </span><del>portability</del><ins>a method that presumes one language</ins><span class="eq"> is </span><del>analyzed</del><ins>re-derived</ins><span class="eq"> </span><del>via</del><ins>by every adopter on a different stack, and</ins><span class="eq"> the </span><del>CI</del><ins>re-derivation</ins><span class="eq"> </span><del>matrix,</del><ins>is</ins><span class="eq"> </span><del>not</del><ins>where</ins><span class="eq"> </span><del>a</del><ins>the</ins><span class="eq"> </span><del>single</del><ins>traceability</ins><span class="eq"> </span><del>unit</del><ins>guarantees</ins><span class="eq"> </span><del>test.</del><ins>get dropped. Shipping per-stack variants was rejected: it multiplies the surface that must stay consistent.</ins></div><div class="cellname">AcceptanceCriteria <span class="pill">0% of the words changed</span></div><div class="diff"><span class="eq">The</span><del> CI matrix spans Linux, Windows and macOS on Python 3.11 and latest (3.x) and is green; macOS runs on current Python (3.x) only — the 3.11 floor is a platform-agnostic language/stdlib guarantee already exercised on Linux and Windows, while macOS&#x27;s job is OS-specific behavior (fcntl.flock, paths, git worktrees) that does not vary by Python version, so the macOS+3.11 cell is excluded as a redundant-coverage call (M-27), not a runner-availability workaround (3.11 has arm64 macOS builds); the</del><span class="eq"> ID scheme is language-neutral.</span></div><div class="ctx"><div class="ctxhead">the rest of this SR — unchanged since the baseline</div><div class="field"><span class="k">SR-ID</span><span class="v">SR-035</span></div><div class="field"><span class="k">Title</span><span class="v">Stack-agnostic across OSes</span></div><div class="field"><span class="k">SN-Refs</span><span class="v">SN-003;SN-011</span></div><div class="field"><span class="k">Priority</span><span class="v">M</span></div><div class="field"><span class="k">Verification</span><span class="v">Analysis</span></div><div class="field"><span class="k">Status</span><span class="v">Modified</span></div><div class="field"><span class="k">Phase</span><span class="v">1</span></div><div class="field"><span class="k">Area</span><span class="v">Portability</span></div></div></div><div class="row"><div class="row-head"><span class="rid">TC TC-035</span><span class="pill">changed</span></div><div class="cellname">Verifies <span class="pill">100% of the words changed</span></div><div class="diff"><del>SR-035</del><ins>SR-035;SR-114</ins></div><div class="cellname">Expected <span class="pill">40% of the words changed</span></div><div class="diff"><span class="eq">Satisfies SR-035 </span><ins>and SR-114 </ins><span class="eq">AcceptanceCriteria</span></div><div class="ctx"><div class="ctxhead">the rest of this TC — unchanged since the baseline</div><div class="field"><span class="k">TC-ID</span><span class="v">TC-035</span></div><div class="field"><span class="k">Level</span><span class="v">Analysis</span></div><div class="field"><span class="k">Method</span><span class="v">Analyze the CI matrix result across Linux/Windows/macOS x Python 3.11/latest.</span></div><div class="field"><span class="k">Tier</span><span class="v">Full</span></div><div class="field"><span class="k">Automated</span><span class="v">Yes</span></div><div class="field"><span class="k">Evidence</span><span class="v">.github/workflows/test.yml</span></div><div class="field"><span class="k">Status</span><span class="v">Verified</span></div><div class="field"><span class="k">Phase</span><span class="v">1</span></div></div></div></article><article class="card" id="SR-040-attest"><h3><span class="rid">SR-040</span><span>Per-phase routing and review dial</span><span class="pill">re-attest owed</span></h3><p class="baseline">baseline a5052a913 (2026-07-25) — from --since</p><div class="row"><div class="row-head"><span class="rid">SR SR-040</span><span class="pill">changed</span></div><div class="cellname">Rationale <span class="pill">81% of the words changed</span></div><div class="diff"><span class="eq">Realizes SN-006 and SN-016 — </span><del>the AGENT_ROLES R1/R3/R6 build calls: cross-family review routing is first-class (two</del><ins>two</ins><span class="eq"> samples of one model share blind </span><del>spots;</del><ins>spots, so a review by the family that built the change agrees with it for the wrong reasons;</ins><span class="eq"> cross-family </span><ins>routing </ins><span class="eq">is</span><ins> what makes</ins><span class="eq"> the </span><del>recommended</del><ins>second</ins><span class="eq"> </span><del>review-policy</del><ins>opinion</ins><span class="eq"> </span><del>2</del><ins>independent,</ins><span class="eq"> </span><del>pairing),</del><ins>and</ins><span class="eq"> </span><del>review</del><ins>one</ins><span class="eq"> </span><del>dispatch</del><ins>model for every phase was rejected on that basis. Dispatch</ins><span class="eq"> stays </span><del>the zero-code in-process-phase convention (rekeyed</del><ins>keyed</ins><span class="eq"> off the </span><del>SR-059-deleted</del><ins>in-process</ins><span class="eq"> </span><del>docs/run-phase</del><ins>session</ins><span class="eq"> </span><del>by</del><ins>phase</ins><span class="eq"> </span><del>WI-207,</del><ins>because</ins><span class="eq"> </span><del>audit-108</del><ins>the</ins><span class="eq"> </span><del>finding</del><ins>alternative,</ins><span class="eq"> </span><del>1),</del><ins>a per-phase code branch, makes adding a phase a code change</ins><span class="eq"> and </span><del>the</del><ins>so discourages adding one. The resume surface&#x27;s growth tripwire warns rather than fails because a growing</ins><span class="eq"> resume surface </span><del>has</del><ins>is</ins><span class="eq"> a </span><del>warn-only</del><ins>smell</ins><span class="eq"> </span><del>growth</del><ins>and</ins><span class="eq"> </span><del>tripwire.</del><ins>not a defect, and failing on a smell trains an operator to bypass the check.</ins></div><div class="cellname">AcceptanceCriteria <span class="pill">15% of the words changed</span></div><div class="diff"><span class="eq">A mapped session phase invokes its own command template and the default template does not fire; a broken map entry fails preflight before iteration 1; the banner surfaces </span><del>docs/review-policy;</del><ins>the reviewer dial from docs/process.toml [policies] review_rounds;</ins><span class="eq"> an oversized status.md warns on stderr while the run proceeds; AGENT_STATUS_WARN_BYTES=0 silences.</span></div><div class="ctx"><div class="ctxhead">the rest of this SR — unchanged since the baseline</div><div class="field"><span class="k">SR-ID</span><span class="v">SR-040</span></div><div class="field"><span class="k">Title</span><span class="v">Per-phase routing and review dial</span></div><div class="field"><span class="k">SN-Refs</span><span class="v">SN-006;SN-016</span></div><div class="field"><span class="k">Requirement</span><span class="v">The unattended coordinator shall select the agent command template per in-process session phase (PLAN/BUILD/REVIEW-A/REVIEW-B/DESIGN-CHECK/CRITIQUE - the coordinator&#x27;s own activity; the retired docs/run-phase file, deleted by SR-059, is not an input) via AGENT_CMD_MAP/--cmd-map, falling back to the single AGENT_CMD; surface the declared reviewer dial (docs/review-policy, default 1) at run start without enforcing it; and warn (never block) when a lane resume surface exceeds the declared size threshold.</span></div><div class="field"><span class="k">Priority</span><span class="v">M</span></div><div class="field"><span class="k">Verification</span><span class="v">Test</span></div><div class="field"><span class="k">Status</span><span class="v">Modified</span></div><div class="field"><span class="k">Phase</span><span class="v">1</span></div><div class="field"><span class="k">Area</span><span class="v">Unattended loop</span></div></div></div></article><article class="card" id="SR-057-attest"><h3><span class="rid">SR-057</span><span>WI-DAG frontier scheduling</span><span class="pill">re-attest owed</span></h3><p class="baseline">baseline a5052a913 (2026-07-25) — from --since</p><div class="row"><div class="row-head"><span class="rid">SR SR-057</span><span class="pill">changed</span></div><div class="cellname">SN-Refs <span class="pill">100% of the words changed</span></div><div class="diff"><del>SN-025;SN-006</del><ins>SN-025;SN-027;SN-006</ins></div><div class="cellname">Requirement <span class="pill">29% of the words changed</span></div><div class="diff"><span class="eq">A stdlib schedule.py library/CLI shall derive the dependency-ready frontier from the tracked WI registry plus </span><del>dispatcher</del><ins>the</ins><span class="eq"> </span><del>reservations</del><ins>active claims</ins><span class="eq"> - never from prose - excluding </span><del>blocked/deferred/reserved/protected-conflicting/exclusive-conflicting</del><ins>blocked (queued + blockref), deferred, claimed, protected-conflicting and exclusive-conflicting</ins><span class="eq"> WIs, and</span><del> shall order eligible traincars deterministically by (gate class, Priority desc, transitive downstream-dependent count desc, remaining hard-path length desc, first WI id),</del><span class="eq"> exposing ready --explain, ready --format </span><del>json,</del><ins>json</ins><span class="eq"> and simulate --jobs N.</span></div><div class="cellname">Rationale <span class="pill">84% of the words changed</span></div><div class="diff"><span class="eq">Realizes SN-025 </span><del>-</del><ins>and SN-006 —</ins><span class="eq"> readiness </span><ins>read from prose </ins><span class="eq">is </span><del>derived</del><ins>a</ins><span class="eq"> </span><del>and</del><ins>decision</ins><span class="eq"> </span><del>inspectable</del><ins>nobody can reproduce,</ins><span class="eq"> so the </span><del>same</del><ins>validator,</ins><span class="eq"> </span><del>scheduling</del><ins>the</ins><span 