v class="field"><span class="k">CodeSymbol</span><span class="v">_first_declared_line</span></div><div class="field"><span class="k">Detail</span><span class="v">The single first-non-comment-line reader the hooks, agent_loop.read_declared, and check_privacy all use so a declared policy value is read one way.</span></div><div class="field"><span class="k">Status</span><span class="v">Verified</span></div><div class="field"><span class="k">Component</span><span class="v">CMP-004</span></div><div class="field"><span class="k">Phase</span><span class="v">1</span></div></div></div><div class="row"><div class="row-head"><span class="rid">TC TC-031</span><span class="pill">changed</span></div><div class="cellname">Verifies <span class="pill">100% of the words changed</span></div><div class="diff"><del>SR-031;LLR-031</del><ins>SR-031; LLR-031</ins></div><div class="cellname">Method <span class="pill">88% of the words changed</span></div><div class="diff"><span class="eq">Run the </span><del>gate-policy</del><ins>process-config</ins><span class="eq"> and </span><del>push-policy</del><ins>policy</ins><span class="eq"> </span><del>suites;</del><ins>suites:</ins><span class="eq"> </span><del>each</del><ins>every</ins><span class="eq"> </span><del>reader</del><ins>enforcer</ins><span class="eq"> </span><del>returns</del><ins>reads one value per dial from docs/process.toml,</ins><span class="eq"> the </span><del>first</del><ins>hooks&#x27;</ins><span class="eq"> </span><del>declared</del><ins>sh</ins><span class="eq"> </span><del>line.</del><ins>and tomllib agree over the adversarial shape table, and a mixed config is refused.</ins></div><div class="ctx"><div class="ctxhead">the rest of this TC — unchanged since the baseline</div><div class="field"><span class="k">TC-ID</span><span class="v">TC-031</span></div><div class="field"><span class="k">Level</span><span class="v">Integration</span></div><div class="field"><span class="k">Tier</span><span class="v">Full</span></div><div class="field"><span class="k">Expected</span><span class="v">Satisfies SR-031 AcceptanceCriteria</span></div><div class="field"><span class="k">Automated</span><span class="v">Yes</span></div><div class="field"><span class="k">Evidence</span><span class="v">tests/test_gate_policy.py;tests/test_push_policy.py</span></div><div class="field"><span class="k">Status</span><span class="v">Modified</span></div><div class="field"><span class="k">Phase</span><span class="v">1</span></div></div></div></article><article class="card" id="SR-034-attest"><h3><span class="rid">SR-034</span><span>Kit scripts run on stdlib plus ledger-declared dependencies</span><span class="pill">re-attest owed</span></h3><p class="baseline">baseline a5052a913 (2026-07-25) — from --since</p><div class="row"><div class="row-head"><span class="rid">SR SR-034</span><span class="pill">changed</span></div><div class="cellname">Title <span class="pill">100% of the words changed</span></div><div class="diff"><del>Scripts</del><ins>Kit</ins><span class="eq"> </span><del>are</del><ins>scripts</ins><span class="eq"> </span><del>stdlib-only</del><ins>run on stdlib plus ledger-declared dependencies</ins></div><div class="cellname">Requirement <span class="pill">58% of the words changed</span></div><div class="diff"><span class="eq">Every kit script shall run on a clean Python 3.11+ </span><del>with</del><ins>using</ins><span class="eq"> </span><del>no</del><ins>the</ins><span class="eq"> </span><del>pip installs (standard</del><ins>standard</ins><span class="eq"> library </span><del>only).</del><ins>plus only those non-stdlib dependencies declared as a reviewed row in docs/dependencies.md.</ins></div><div class="cellname">Rationale <span class="pill">81% of the words changed</span></div><div class="diff"><span class="eq">Realizes SN-011 — the kit </span><del>imposes</del><ins>must impose</ins><span class="eq"> no</span><ins> *unargued*</ins><span class="eq"> dependency stack on a downstream repo to run its </span><del>checks.</del><ins>checks, but a blanket ban is itself a design constraint that can force a worse hand-rolled alternative than a well-chosen tool, so the bar is a reviewed argument per dependency (owner RULING-3, 2026-07-28), not abstinence. Leaving the row at &quot;stdlib-only&quot; was rejected: it had already drifted from the standing ruling, leaving the registry and the ledger giving two answers to one question.</ins></div><div class="cellname">AcceptanceCriteria <span class="pill">88% of the words changed</span></div><div class="diff"><del>No kit script imports a third-party package; an</del><ins>An</ins><span class="eq"> AST scan </span><del>asserts</del><ins>of scripts/*.py resolves</ins><span class="eq"> every top-level import </span><del>in scripts/*.py resolves </del><span class="eq">to </span><del>stdlib</del><ins>stdlib, a local sibling,</ins><span class="eq"> or a </span><del>local</del><ins>Kind=python</ins><span class="eq"> </span><del>sibling.</del><ins>row in docs/dependencies.md; an undeclared non-stdlib import fails the suite; every declared row names what it replaces, why hand-rolling is worse, and the ruling that admitted it; a shipped-tier row (one an adopter is forced to install) exists only with an owner ruling recorded in the ledger, stdlib remaining preferred there.</ins></div><div class="ctx"><div class="ctxhead">the rest of this SR — unchanged since the baseline</div><div class="field"><span class="k">SR-ID</span><span class="v">SR-034</span></div><div class="field"><span class="k">SN-Refs</span><span class="v">SN-011</span></div><div class="field"><span class="k">Priority</span><span class="v">M</span></div><div class="field"><span class="k">Verification</span><span class="v">Analysis</span></div><div class="field"><span class="k">Status</span><span class="v">Modified</span></div><div class="field"><span class="k">Phase</span><span class="v">1</span></div><div class="field"><span class="k">Area</span><span class="v">Portability</s